{
  "title": "7: al-Aa'raaf الأعراف",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nالۤمّۤصۤ‏(1)\n\nAlif, Laam, Meem, Saad.\nكِتٰبٌ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْكَ فَلَا يَكُنْ فِىْ صَدْرِكَ حَرَجٌ مِّنْهُ لِتُنْذِرَ بِهٖ وَذِكْرٰى لِلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(2)\n\n(The) Book (the Qur’an) hath been sent down unto thee so that there be no straintendness or narrowness in thy breast about it, that thou mayest warn thereby (and it be) a reminder to the believers.\nاِتَّبِعُوْا مَاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْكُمْ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ وَلَا تَتَّبِعُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِهٖۤ اَوْلِيَآءَ ؕ قَلِيْلًا مَّا تَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(3)\n\n(O’ people!) Follow ye what hath been sent down unto you from your Lord, and follow ye not (any) other than Him, as (Your) guardians (or friends)’, How little do ye mind.\nوَكَمْ مِّنْ قَرْيَةٍ اَهْلَكْنٰهَا فَجَآءَهَا بَاْسُنَا بَيَاتًا اَوْ هُمْ قَآئِلُوْنَ‏(4)\n\nAnd how many a town have We destroyed, Our wrath came unto them by night or while they reposed themselves at noonday.\nفَمَا كَانَ دَعْوٰٮهُمْ اِذْ جَآءَهُمْ بَاْسُنَاۤ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ قَالُوْۤا اِنَّا كُنَّا ظٰلِمِيْنَ‏(5)\n\nSo their cry, when Our wrath came unto them, was not but said they; “Verily we were unjust.\nفَلَنَسْئَلَنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اُرْسِلَ اِلَيْهِمْ وَلَنَسْئَلَنَّ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ ۙ‏(6)\n\nThen certainly will We question those unto whom (Our apostles) were sent, and certainly will We also question the sent ones.\nفَلَنَقُصَّنَّ عَلَيْهِمْ بِعِلْمٍ وَّمَا كُنَّا غَآئِبِيْنَ‏(7)\n\nThen certainly will We relate to them with knowledge for We were not absent.\nوَالْوَزْنُ يَوْمَئِذِ اۨلْحَقُّ ۚ فَمَنْ ثَقُلَتْ مَوَازِيْنُهٗ فَاُولٰۤئِكَ هُمُ الْمُفْلِحُوْنَ‏(8)\n\nAnd the measuring (of the deeds) that day will be just; so whomsoever’s weight be heavy those are they who shall be successful.\nوَمَنْ خَفَّتْ مَوَازِيْنُهٗ فَاُولٰۤئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ خَسِرُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ بِمَا كَانُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا يَظْلِمُوْنَ‏(9)\n\nAnd those whose measure (of the deeds) is light, those are they whose souls suffer loss for what they, with Our signs, did behave unjustly.\nوَلَقَدْ مَكَّنّٰكُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَجَعَلْنَا لَكُمْ فِيْهَا مَعَايِشَ ؕ قَلِيْلًا مَّا تَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(10)\n\nAnd indeed, We have made you inhabit in the earth, and have made We, the means of livelihood for you in it; little it is that ye give thanks.\nوَلَقَدْ خَلَقْنٰكُمْ ثُمَّ صَوَّرْنٰكُمْ ثُمَّ قُلْنَا لِلْمَلٰۤئِكَةِ اسْجُدُوْا لِاٰدَمَ ۖ  فَسَجَدُوْۤا اِلَّاۤ اِبْلِيْسَؕ لَمْ يَكُنْ مِّنَ السّٰجِدِيْنَ‏(11)\n\nAnd indeed We did create you, then We did fashion you, then said We unto the angels; “Prostrate yourselves unto Adam;” so they all did prostrate themselves except Iblees; he was not of the prostrating ones.\nقَالَ مَا مَنَعَكَ اَلَّا تَسْجُدَ اِذْ اَمَرْتُكَ ؕ قَالَ اَنَا خَيْرٌ مِّنْهُ ۚ خَلَقْتَنِىْ مِنْ نَّارٍ وَّخَلَقْتَهٗ مِنْ طِيْنٍ‏(12)\n\nSaid He: “What preventeth thee that thou didst not prostrate when I did command thee?” said he “I am better than him, me hast thou created of fire while thou didst create him (Adam) of clay.\nقَالَ فَاهْبِطْ مِنْهَا فَمَا يَكُوْنُ لَكَ اَنْ تَتَكَبَّرَ فِيْهَا فَاخْرُجْ اِنَّكَ مِنَ الصّٰغِرِيْنَ‏(13)\n\nSaid He: Get thee down hence for it doth not befit thee to behave proudly therein. Get thee out; verily thou art of the despised ones.\nقَالَ اَنْظِرْنِىْۤ اِلٰى يَوْمِ يُبْعَثُوْنَ‏(14)\n\nSaid he: “Grant me respite until the day when they are raised up (resurrected).\nقَالَ اِنَّكَ مِنَ الْمُنْظَرِيْنَ‏(15)\n\nHe said: “Verily thou shalt be of the respited ones.\nقَالَ فَبِمَاۤ اَغْوَيْتَنِىْ لَاَقْعُدَنَّ لَهُمْ صِرَاطَكَ الْمُسْتَقِيْمَۙ‏(16)\n\nSaid he: “As Thou hast deprived me, surely will I lay wait for them in Thy straight (right) path.\nثُمَّ لَاَتِيَنَّهُمْ مِّنْۢ بَيْنِ اَيْدِيْهِمْ وَمِنْ خَلْفِهِمْ وَعَنْ اَيْمَانِهِمْ وَعَنْ شَمَآئِلِهِمْؕ وَلَاٰ تَجِدُ اَكْثَرَهُمْ شٰكِرِيْنَ‏(17)\n\nThen will I surely come upon them from before them, and from behind them and from their right side and from their left side; and Thou wilt not find most of them thankful.\nقَالَ اخْرُجْ مِنْهَا مَذْءُوْمًا مَّدْحُوْرًا ؕ لَمَنْ تَبِعَكَ مِنْهُمْ لَاَمْلَئَنَّ جَهَنَّمَ مِنْكُمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَ‏(18)\n\nHe said; “Get thee out of this (state), despised, driven away; whosoever of them followeth thee, certainly will I fill the hell with you all.\nوَيٰۤاٰدَمُ اسْكُنْ اَنْتَ وَزَوْجُكَ الْجَنَّةَ فَكُلَا مِنْ حَيْثُ شِئْتُمَا وَلَا تَقْرَبَا هٰذِهِ الشَّجَرَةَ فَتَكُوْنَا مِنَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(19)\n\nAnd O’ Adam! Dwell thou and thy wife in the garden, so eat ye two from wherever ye two desire, but go not ye two nigh into this tree for then ye two will be of the unjust.\nفَوَسْوَسَ لَهُمَا الشَّيْطٰنُ لِيُبْدِىَ لَهُمَا مَا وٗرِىَ عَنْهُمَا مِنْ سَوْاٰتِهِمَا وَقَالَ مَا نَهٰٮكُمَا رَبُّكُمَا عَنْ هٰذِهِ الشَّجَرَةِ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ تَكُوْنَا مَلَكَيْنِ اَوْ تَكُوْنَا مِنَ الْخٰلِدِيْنَ‏(20)\n\nThen whispered Satan evil suggestions unto the two (Adam and Eve) that he might display unto them what hath been kept hidden from them of their shame, and said he: “Forbade not ye two, your Lord from this tree save lest ye two may become angels or lest ye two may become the immortals.\nوَقَاسَمَهُمَاۤ اِنِّىْ لَكُمَا لَمِنَ النّٰصِحِيْنَۙ‏(21)\n\nAnd he swore unto them both: “Verily I am unto you a sincere adviser.\nفَدَلّٰٮهُمَا بِغُرُوْرٍ ۚ فَلَمَّا ذَاقَا الشَّجَرَةَ بَدَتْ لَهُمَا سَوْءٰتُهُمَا وَطَفِقَا يَخْصِفٰنِ عَلَيْهِمَا مِنْ وَّرَقِ الْجَنَّةِ ؕ وَنَادٰٮهُمَا رَبُّهُمَاۤ اَلَمْ اَنْهَكُمَا عَنْ تِلْكُمَا الشَّجَرَةِ وَاَقُلْ لَّكُمَاۤ اِنَّ الشَّيْطٰنَ لَكُمَا عَدُوٌّ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(22)\n\nThen he instigated them both by deceit so when they tasted (of) the tree their shameful things got displayed unto them, and they both began covering themselves with the leaves of the Garden; and called out unto them their Lord (saying): “Did I not forbid ye two that tree, and (did I not) say unto you both that Satan is of ye both a declared enemy?\nقَالَا رَبَّنَا ظَلَمْنَاۤ اَنْفُسَنَا وَاِنْ لَّمْ تَغْفِرْ لَنَا وَتَرْحَمْنَا لَنَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الْخٰسِرِيْنَ‏(23)\n\nSaid they “O’ Our Lord! Unjust have we been unto ourselves, and if Thou forgive us not and deal (not) with mercy unto us (then), We will certainly be of the losers.\nقَالَ اهْبِطُوْا بَعْضُكُمْ لِبَعْضٍ عَدُوٌّ ۚ وَلَكُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ مُسْتَقَرٌّ وَّمَتَاعٌ اِلٰى حِيْنٍ‏(24)\n\nHe said: “Get ye down, some of you (being) the enemies of the others; and for you there is in the earth an abode and a provision (of sustenance) for a (fixed) time.\nقَالَ فِيْهَا تَحْيَوْنَ وَفِيْهَا تَمُوْتُوْنَ وَمِنْهَا تُخْرَجُوْنَ‏(25)\n\n(And) said He: “Therein ye shall live, and therein shall ye die, and from it ye shall be brought out.\nيٰبَنِىْۤ اٰدَمَ قَدْ اَنْزَلْنَا عَلَيْكُمْ لِبَاسًا يُّوَارِىْ سَوْاٰتِكُمْ وَرِيْشًا ؕ وَلِبَاسُ التَّقْوٰى ۙ ذٰ لِكَ خَيْرٌ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ مِنْ اٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَذَّكَّرُوْنَ‏(26)\n\nO’ children of Adam! Indeed We have sent down unto you raiment to cover your shame and (for) adornment and the raiment of piety, that is the best; this is of the signs of God that ye may be mindful.\nيٰبَنِىْۤ اٰدَمَ لَا يَفْتِنَنَّكُمُ الشَّيْطٰنُ كَمَاۤ اَخْرَجَ اَبَوَيْكُمْ مِّنَ الْجَنَّةِ يَنْزِعُ عَنْهُمَا لِبَاسَهُمَا لِيُرِيَهُمَا سَوْءاٰتِهِمَا ؕ اِنَّهٗ يَرٰٮكُمْ هُوَ وَقَبِيْلُهٗ مِنْ حَيْثُ لَا تَرَوْنَهُمْ ؕ اِنَّا جَعَلْنَا الشَّيٰطِيْنَ اَوْلِيَآءَ لِلَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(27)\n\nO’ children of Adam! Let not Satan involve you into affliction as he got your parents out, from the garden (of the blissful life) stripping off their raiment, that he may expose unto them their shame; He watcheth you, he and (also) his tribe, from whence ye see them not; Verily We have made the devils to be the guardians of those who believe not.\nوَاِذَا فَعَلُوْا فَاحِشَةً قَالُوْا وَجَدْنَا عَلَيْهَاۤ اٰبَآءَنَا وَاللّٰهُ اَمَرَنَا بِهَا ؕ قُلْ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَاْمُرُ بِالْفَحْشَآءِ ؕ اَتَقُوْلُوْنَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ مَا لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(28)\n\nAnd when they act lewdness say they: “We found our fathers (acting) upon this, and God hath enjoined it on us,” Say: (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “Verily God enjoineth not lewdness; Do ye say against God what ye know not?\nقُلْ اَمَرَ رَبِّىْ بِالْقِسْطِ وَاَقِيْمُوْا وُجُوْهَكُمْ عِنْدَ كُلِّ مَسْجِدٍ وَّادْعُوْهُ مُخْلِصِيْنَ لَهُ الدِّيْنَ    ؕ كَمَا بَدَاَكُمْ تَعُوْدُوْنَؕ‏(29)\n\nSay thou: “My Lord hath enjoined justice and set ye upright your faces at (each time and place) of prostration, and call upon Him, being sincere exclusively unto Him in religion; even as He brought you forth (in the beginning) so unto Him shall ye also return.\nفَرِيْقًا هَدٰى وَ فَرِيْقًا حَقَّ عَلَيْهِمُ الضَّلٰلَةُ  ؕ اِنَّهُمُ اتَّخَذُوا الشَّيٰطِيْنَ اَوْلِيَآءَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ وَيَحْسَبُوْنَ اَنَّهُمْ مُّهْتَدُوْنَ‏(30)\n\nA party He hath guided aright, and (the other) party entitled themselves to error; (for) verily they took the devils for their guardians other than God, and think they, that they are the ones guided aright.\nيٰبَنِىْۤ اٰدَمَ خُذُوْا زِيْنَتَكُمْ عِنْدَ كُلِّ مَسْجِدٍ وَّكُلُوْا وَاشْرَبُوْا وَلَا تُسْرِفُوْا ۚ اِنَّهٗ لَا يُحِبُّ الْمُسْرِفِيْنَ‏(31)\n\nO’ children of Adam! Be ye adorned at every time of prostration and eat ye and drink ye and commit ye not excesses; Verily He (God) loveth not the extravagants.\nقُلْ مَنْ حَرَّمَ زِيْنَةَ اللّٰهِ الَّتِىْۤ اَخْرَجَ لِعِبَادِهٖ وَالطَّيِّبٰتِ مِنَ الرِّزْقِؕ قُلْ هِىَ لِلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا خَالِصَةً يَّوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِؕ كَذٰلِكَ نُفَصِّلُ الْاٰيٰتِ لِقَوْمٍ يَّعْلَمُوْنَ‏(32)\n\nSay: (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “Who hath prohibited the adornment (granted) of God, which He hath brought forth for His servants and the good things of the provisions?” Say: “These are for those who believe, in the (short) life of this world (to he) exclusively theirs on the Day of Judgment;” Thus do We explain in details the signs for a people who know.\nقُلْ اِنَّمَا حَرَّمَ رَبِّىَ الْفَوَاحِشَ مَا ظَهَرَ مِنْهَا وَمَا بَطَنَ وَ الْاِثْمَ وَالْبَغْىَ بِغَيْرِ الْحَقِّ وَاَنْ تُشْرِكُوْا بِاللّٰهِ مَا لَمْ يُنَزِّلْ بِهٖ سُلْطٰنًا وَّاَنْ تَقُوْلُوْا عَلَى اللّٰهِ مَا لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(33)\n\nSay: “Verily did prohibit my Lord only shameful deeds, those apparent of them and those concealed, and sin and rebellion without (any) right, and that ye associate (not) with God for which hath not been sent down any authority, and that ye say (not) against God what ye know not.\nوَلِكُلِّ اُمَّةٍ اَجَلٌۚ فَاِذَا جَآءَ اَجَلُهُمْ لَا يَسْتَاْخِرُوْنَ سَاعَةً وَّلَا يَسْتَقْدِمُوْنَ‏(34)\n\nAnd for every people is (an appointed) term, so when cometh their (appointed) term, they shall not remain behind an hour (even for the least while) nor can they go before.\nيٰبَنِىْۤ اٰدَمَ اِمَّا يَاْتِيَنَّكُمْ رُسُلٌ مِّنْكُمْ يَقُصُّوْنَ عَلَيْكُمْ اٰيٰتِىْۙ فَمَنِ اتَّقٰى وَاَصْلَحَ فَلَا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا هُمْ يَحْزَنُوْنَ‏(35)\n\nO’ children of Adam! When come unto you apostles from among you, relating unto you My signs, then whosoever guardeth himself against evil and amendeth (himself), then no fear shall come upon them, nor shall they be grieved.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَاسْتَكْبَرُوْا عَنْهَاۤ اُولٰۤئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ النَّارِۚ هُمْ فِيْهَا خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(36)\n\nAnd those who belie our signs and in pride turn away from them, these are the inmates of the (Hell) fire, and they shall abide therein.\nفَمَنْ اَظْلَمُ مِمَّنِ افْتَرٰى عَلَى اللّٰهِ كَذِبًا اَوْ كَذَّبَ بِاٰيٰتِهٖ ؕ اُولٰۤئِكَ يَنَالُهُمْ نَصِيْبُهُمْ مِّنَ الْكِتٰبِؕ حَتّٰٓى اِذَا جَآءَتْهُمْ رُسُلُنَا يَتَوَفَّوْنَهُمْ ۙ قَالُوْۤا اَيْنَ مَا كُنْتُمْ تَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ ؕ قَالُوْا ضَلُّوْا عَنَّا وَشَهِدُوْا عَلٰٓى اَنْفُسِهِمْ اَنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا كٰفِرِيْنَ‏(37)\n\nWho is then more unjust than he who orget a lie against God or belieth His signs? Those (are they) unto whom shall reach their share (as decreed) in the Book; until come unto them Our messengers, cause them to die, they (would) say: “Where is that which ye did call upon besides God?” They would say “They have left us away in the lurch,” and they shall bear witness against themselves that they had been infidels.\nقَالَ ادْخُلُوْا فِىْۤ اُمَمٍ قَدْ خَلَتْ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ مِّنَ الْجِنِّ وَالْاِنْسِ فِى النَّارِ ؕ كُلَّمَا دَخَلَتْ اُمَّةٌ لَّعَنَتْ اُخْتَهَا ؕ حَتّٰۤى اِذَا ادَّارَكُوْا فِيْهَا جَمِيْعًا ۙ قَالَتْ اُخْرٰٮهُمْ لِاُوْلٰٮهُمْ رَبَّنَا هٰٓؤُلَۤاءِ اَضَلُّوْنَا فَاٰتِهِمْ عَذَابًا ضِعْفًا مِّنَ النَّارِ  ؕ قَالَ لِكُلٍّ ضِعْفٌ وَّلٰكِنْ لَّا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(38)\n\nHe will say: “Enter ye among the people who indeed have passed away before you, of jinn and men into the (Hell) fire; Every time a (new) people entereth (it) it shall curse its sister (people); until they have all come together into it, the later of them shall say about the former of them; “O’ Our Lord! These are they who led us astray, therefore give them a double chastisement of the fire;” He will say: “For everyone (of you) double, but ye know.\nوَقَالَتْ اُوْلٰٮهُمْ لِاُخْرٰٮهُمْ فَمَا كَانَ لَكُمْ عَلَيْنَا مِنْ فَضْلٍ فَذُوْقُوا الْعَذَابَ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(39)\n\nAnd the former of them will say to the later of them “So (now) there is not for you any advantage over us, therefore taste ye the chastisement for what ye earned.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَاسْتَكْبَرُوْا عَنْهَا لَا تُفَتَّحُ لَهُمْ اَبْوَابُ السَّمَآءِ وَلَا يَدْخُلُوْنَ الْجَنَّةَ حَتّٰى يَلِجَ الْجَمَلُ فِىْ سَمِّ الْخِيَاطِ ؕ وَكَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(40)\n\nVerily those who belie Our signs and in pride turn away from them, shall not open for them the gates of heaven nor shall they enter the Garden (of Paradise) until the camel passeth through the eye of the needle; thus do We recompense the guilty.\nلَهُمْ مِّنْ جَهَنَّمَ مِهَادٌ وَّمِنْ فَوْقِهِمْ غَوَاشٍ ؕ وَكَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(41)\n\nFor them shall be the bed of the (Hell) fire and from above them the covering (of it); Thus do We recompense the unjust.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ لَا نُكَلِّفُ نَفْسًا اِلَّا وُسْعَهَاۤ  اُولٰۤئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ الْجَنَّةِۚ هُمْ فِيْهَا خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(42)\n\nAnd those who believe and do good deeds, task We not any soul but to its ability, they are the dwellers of the Garden of (Bliss); They, in it shall abide.\nوَنَزَعْنَا مَا فِىْ صُدُوْرِهِمْ مِّنْ غِلٍّ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهِمُ الْاَنْهٰرُۚ وَقَالُوا الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِىْ هَدٰٮنَا لِهٰذَا وَمَا كُنَّا لِنَهْتَدِىَ لَوْلَاۤ اَنْ هَدٰٮنَا اللّٰهُ ۚ لَقَدْ جَآءَتْ رُسُلُ رَبِّنَا بِالْحَقِّ ؕ وَنُوْدُوْۤا اَنْ تِلْكُمُ الْجَنَّةُ اُوْرِثْتُمُوْهَا بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(43)\n\nAnd We will remove whatever rancour be in their breast, there shall flow beneath their abodes rivers, and they will say: “All praise be (only) to God who guided us to this and We would not have been guided had not God guided us; Indeed, did come the apostles of Our Lord with the truth;” and it shall be cried out unto them that: “(Behold!) This is the Garden of which ye are made heirs for what ye did.\nوَنَادٰٓى اَصْحٰبُ الْجَنَّةِ اَصْحٰبَ النَّارِ اَنْ قَدْ وَجَدْنَا مَا وَعَدَنَا رَبُّنَا حَقًّا فَهَلْ وَجَدْتُّمْ مَّا وَعَدَ رَبُّكُمْ حَقًّا ؕ قَالُوْا نَعَمْ ۚ فَاَذَّنَ مُؤَذِّنٌۢ بَيْنَهُمْ اَنْ لَّعْنَةُ اللّٰهِ عَلَى الظّٰلِمِيْنَۙ‏(44)\n\nAnd will call out of the inmates of the Garden (of Paradise) unto the inmates of the (Hell) fire (saying); “Indeed we have found what promised us Our Lord to be true; have ye too found what promised your Lord, to be true?” They will say: “Yes.” Then a crier will cry out between them that “The curse of God is on the unjust.\nالَّذِيْنَ يَصُدُّوْنَ عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَيَبْغُوْنَهَا عِوَجًا ۚ وَهُمْ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ كٰفِرُوْنَۘ‏(45)\n\nThose who hinder (People) from the path of God and seek to make it crooked, and they in the hereafter disbelieve.\nوَبَيْنَهُمَا حِجَابٌۚ وَعَلَى الْاَعْرَافِ رِجَالٌ يَّعْرِفُوْنَ كُلًّاۢ بِسِيْمٰٮهُمْ ۚ وَنَادَوْا اَصْحٰبَ الْجَنَّةِ اَنْ سَلٰمٌ عَلَيْكُمْ لَمْ يَدْخُلُوْهَا وَهُمْ يَطْمَعُوْنَ‏(46)\n\nAnd between the two shall be a veil and on the heights shall be men who know all by their marks, and they shall call out to the inmates of the Garden (Paradise) “Peace be on you,” They shall not have yet entered it, though they do hope (thereof).\nوَاِذَا صُرِفَتْ اَبْصَارُهُمْ تِلْقَآءَ اَصْحٰبِ النَّارِۙ قَالُوْا رَبَّنَا لَا تَجْعَلْنَا مَعَ الْقَوْمِ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(47)\n\nAnd when (they) will turn their eyes towards the inmates of the (Hell) fire, they shall say: “O’ Our Lord! cause us not to be with the unjust people.\nوَنَادٰٓى اَصْحٰبُ الْاَعْرَافِ رِجَالًا يَّعْرِفُوْنَهُمْ بِسِيْمٰٮهُمْ قَالُوْا مَاۤ اَغْنٰى عَنْكُمْ جَمْعُكُمْ وَمَا كُنْتُمْ تَسْتَكْبِرُوْنَ‏(48)\n\nAnd will call the occupants of the heights unto the inmates of the Hell who can recognise them by their marks; They will say: “Of no avail had been your amassing and what ye used to act proudly.\nاَهٰٓؤُلَۤاءِ الَّذِيْنَ اَقْسَمْتُمْ لَا يَنَالُهُمُ اللّٰهُ بِرَحْمَةٍ ؕ اُدْخُلُوا الْجَنَّةَ لَا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْكُمْ وَلَاۤ اَنْتُمْ تَحْزَنُوْنَ‏(49)\n\n(Behold ye!) “Are these they whom ye swear that God will bestow not His mercy on them? (whom God now sayeth) Enter ye into the Garden (Paradise)! No fear shall be on you nor shall ye grieve.\nوَنَادٰٓى اَصْحٰبُ النَّارِ اَصْحٰبَ الْجَنَّةِ اَنْ اَفِيْضُوْا عَلَيْنَا مِنَ الْمَآءِ اَوْ مِمَّا رَزَقَكُمُ اللّٰهُ ؕ قَالُوْۤا اِنَّ اللّٰهَ حَرَّمَهُمَا عَلَى الْكٰفِرِيْنَ ۙ‏(50)\n\nAnd shall call the inmates of the (Hell) fire unto the inmates of the Garden (of bliss) saying: “Pour on us of the water or of what God hath provided you with; “They shall say: “Verily God hath forbidden both to the infidels.\nالَّذِيْنَ اتَّخَذُوْا دِيْنَهُمْ لَهْوًا وَّلَعِبًا وَّغَرَّتْهُمُ الْحَيٰوةُ الدُّنْيَا ۚ فَالْيَوْمَ نَنْسٰٮهُمْ كَمَا نَسُوْا لِقَآءَ يَوْمِهِمْ هٰذَا ۙ وَمَا كَانُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا يَجْحَدُوْنَ‏(51)\n\n(Those) Who made their religion a past time and play and whom the life of the world hath deceived. So today We neglect them as they did neglect this day of theirs, and as they did deny Our signs.\nوَلَقَدْ جِئْنٰهُمْ بِكِتٰبٍ فَصَّلْنٰهُ عَلٰى عِلْمٍ هُدًى وَّرَحْمَةً لِّقَوْمٍ يُّؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(52)\n\nAnd indeed, We have brought unto them a Book, which We have explained it with know-ledge a guidance and a mercy for people who believe.\nهَلْ يَنْظُرُوْنَ اِلَّا تَاْوِيْلَهٗؕ يَوْمَ يَاْتِىْ تَاْوِيْلُهٗ يَقُوْلُ الَّذِيْنَ نَسُوْهُ مِنْ قَبْلُ قَدْ جَآءَتْ رُسُلُ رَبِّنَا بِالْحَقِّۚ فَهَلْ لَّنَا مِنْ شُفَعَآءَ فَيَشْفَعُوْا لَنَاۤ اَوْ نُرَدُّ فَنَعْمَلَ غَيْرَ الَّذِىْ كُنَّا نَعْمَلُؕ قَدْ خَسِرُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ وَضَلَّ عَنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يَفْتَرُوْنَ‏(53)\n\nDo they wait for anything but the final fulfilment (the resurrection)? On the day the final fulfilment cometh, those who neglected it before will say: “Indeed came the apostles of Our Lord with the truth; are there for us (now) any intercessors that they may intercede for us? Or could we be sent back so that we might act other than what we did act?” Indeed, they have lost their souls, and what they forged hath gone away from them.\nاِنَّ رَبَّكُمُ اللّٰهُ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَ الْاَرْضَ فِىْ سِتَّةِ اَيَّامٍ ثُمَّ اسْتَوٰى عَلَى الْعَرْشِ يُغْشِى الَّيْلَ النَّهَارَ يَطْلُبُهٗ حَثِيْثًا ۙ وَّالشَّمْسَ وَالْقَمَرَ وَالنُّجُوْمَ مُسَخَّرٰتٍۢ بِاَمْرِهٖ ؕ اَلَا لَهُ الْخَلْقُ وَالْاَمْرُ ؕ تَبٰرَكَ اللّٰهُ رَبُّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(54)\n\nVerily your Lord is God who created the heavens and the earth in six days, then established Himself upon the Arsh (throne). He throweth the veil of night over the day, which pursueth it incessantly, and the sun and the moon and the stars, made (absolutely) subservient to His command; Be it known! (that) His is the creation and the command; Blessed is God, the Lord of the worlds.\nاُدْعُوْا رَبَّكُمْ تَضَرُّعًا وَّخُفْيَةً ؕ اِنَّهٗ لَا يُحِبُّ الْمُعْتَدِيْنَ ۚ‏(55)\n\nCall ye on your Lord, humbly and secretly; Verily loveth not God the transgressors.\nوَلَا تُفْسِدُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ بَعْدَ اِصْلَاحِهَا وَادْعُوْهُ خَوْفًا وَّطَمَعًا ؕ اِنَّ رَحْمَتَ اللّٰهِ قَرِيْبٌ مِّنَ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(56)\n\nAnd make ye not mischief in the earth after its reformation, and call ye on Him fearing (His wrath) and Hoping (for His mercy), verily the mercy of God is well-nigh unto those who do good.\nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ يُرْسِلُ الرِّيٰحَ بُشْرًۢا بَيْنَ يَدَىْ رَحْمَتِهٖ ؕ حَتّٰۤى اِذَاۤ اَقَلَّتْ سَحَابًا ثِقَالًا سُقْنٰهُ لِبَلَدٍ مَّيِّتٍ فَاَنْزَلْنَا بِهِ الْمَآءَ فَاَخْرَجْنَا بِهٖ مِنْ كُلِّ الثَّمَرٰتِؕ كَذٰلِكَ نُخْرِجُ الْمَوْتٰى لَعَلَّكُمْ تَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(57)\n\nAnd He it is Who sendeth forth the (heralding) winds bearing good tidings before His mercy; until they bring up laden clouds, We drive it to a land which is dead, then We send down water thereon, then bring forth with it of fruits of all kinds; Thus will we bring forth the dead that ye may be mindful.\nوَالْبَلَدُ الطَّيِّبُ يَخْرُجُ نَبَاتُهٗ بِاِذْنِ رَبِّهٖ ۚ وَالَّذِىْ خَبُثَ لَا يَخْرُجُ اِلَّا نَكِدًا ؕ كَذٰلِكَ نُصَرِّفُ الْاٰيٰتِ لِقَوْمٍ يَّشْكُرُوْنَ‏(58)\n\nAnd the good land, springeth forth its vegetation (in abundance) at the will of its Lord; and that which is bad cometh not forth (from it), (herbage); but scantily Thus do we display Our signs to people who give thanks.\nلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا نُوْحًا اِلٰى قَوْمِهٖ فَقَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ مَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ اِلٰهٍ غَيْرُهٗ ؕ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمْ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ عَظِيْمٍ‏(59)\n\nIndeed, We did send Noah unto his people, so said he: “O’ my people! Worship ye God (alone)’, ye have no god other than Him; Verily I fear for you the chastisement of a dreadful day.\nقَالَ الْمَلَاُ مِنْ قَوْمِهٖۤ اِنَّا لَنَرٰٮكَ فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(60)\n\nSaid the chiefs of his people, “Verily we do see thee in obvious error.\nقَالَ يٰقَوْمِ لَيْسَ بِىْ ضَلٰلَةٌ وَّلٰكِنِّىْ رَسُوْلٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(61)\n\nSaid he: “O’ my people! No error is in me, but I am an apostle from the Lord of the worlds.\nاُبَلِّغُكُمْ رِسٰلٰتِ رَبِّىْ وَاَنْصَحُ لَكُمْ وَاَعْلَمُ مِنَ اللّٰهِ مَا لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(62)\n\nI deliver unto you the messages from my Lord and advise unto you and know from God what ye know not.\nاَوَعَجِبْتُمْ اَنْ جَآءَكُمْ ذِكْرٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ عَلٰى رَجُلٍ مِّنْكُمْ لِيُنْذِرَكُمْ وَلِتَتَّقُوْا وَلَعَلَّكُمْ تُرْحَمُوْنَ‏(63)\n\nOr wonder ye that an admonition hath come unto you from your Lord through a man from among you, that he might warn you and that ye guard (yourselves against evil) and that mercy be done unto you?\nفَكَذَّبُوْهُ فَاَنْجَيْنٰهُ وَالَّذِيْنَ مَعَهٗ فِى الْفُلْكِ وَاَغْرَقْنَا الَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا ؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا قَوْمًا عَمِيْنَ‏(64)\n\nBut they belied him, so We delivered him and those with him in the Ark, and drowned those who belied Our signs; “Verily they were a blind people.\nوَاِلٰى عَادٍ اَخَاهُمْ هُوْدًا ؕ قَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ مَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ اِلٰهٍ غَيْرُهٗ ؕ اَفَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‏(65)\n\nAnd unto (the people of) Ad (we did send) their brother Hud. He said: “O’ my people Serve ye God (alone), ye have no god other than Him; What! will ye not then guard (yourselves against evil?\nقَالَ الْمَلَاُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْ قَوْمِهٖۤ اِنَّا لَنَرٰٮكَ فِىْ سَفَاهَةٍ وَّاِنَّا لَنَظُنُّكَ مِنَ الْكٰذِبِيْنَ‏(66)\n\nSaid the chiefs of those who disbelieved among his people: “Verily we do see thee in folly; and verily we do think thee to be of the liars.\nقَالَ يٰقَوْمِ لَيْسَ بِىْ سَفَاهَةٌ وَّلٰكِنِّىْ رَسُوْلٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(67)\n\nSaid he: “O’ my people! There is no folly in me, but I am an apostle of the Lord of the worlds.\nاُبَلِّغُكُمْ رِسٰلٰتِ رَبِّىْ وَاَنَا لَكُمْ نَاصِحٌ اَمِيْنٌ‏(68)\n\nI deliver unto you the messages of my Lord and I unto you, am a trusted adviser.\nاَوَعَجِبْتُمْ اَنْ جَآءَكُمْ ذِكْرٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ عَلٰى رَجُلٍ مِّنْكُمْ لِيُنْذِرَكُمْ ؕ وَاذْكُرُوْۤا اِذْ جَعَلَكُمْ ۚ خُلَفَآءَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ قَوْمِ نُوْحٍ وَّزَادَكُمْ فِى الْخَلْقِ بَصْۜطَةً فَاذْكُرُوْۤا اٰ لَۤاءَ اللّٰهِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُوْنَ‏(69)\n\nDo ye wonder that an admonition hath come unto you from your Lord through a man from among you, that he might warn you? And remember ye when He made you successors after Noah’s people, and increased you in stature, so remember ye the bounties of God that ye may be successful.\nقَالُوْۤا اَجِئْتَنَا لِنَعْبُدَ اللّٰهَ وَحْدَهٗ وَنَذَرَ مَا كَانَ يَعْبُدُ اٰبَآؤُنَا ۚ فَاْتِنَا بِمَا تَعِدُنَاۤ اِنْ كُنْتَ مِنَ الصّٰدِقِيْنَ‏(70)\n\nSaid they: “Come thou unto us that we may serve God alone and we give up what used our fathers to serve? Then bring that down unto us what thou doth threaten us with, if thou be of the truthful ones.\nقَالَ قَدْ وَقَعَ عَلَيْكُمْ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ رِجْسٌ وَّغَضَبٌؕ اَتُجَادِلُوْنَنِىْ فِىْۤ اَسْمَآءٍ سَمَّيْتُمُوْهَاۤ اَنْتُمْ وَاٰبَآؤُكُمْ مَّا نَزَّلَ اللّٰهُ بِهَا مِنْ سُلْطٰنٍؕ فَانْتَظِرُوْۤا اِنِّىْ مَعَكُمْ مِّنَ الْمُنْتَظِرِيْنَ‏(71)\n\nSaid he: “Indeed hath fallen upon you, from your Lord (His punishment and wrath); what! Dispute ye with me about the names which ye have named them (your idols), ye and your fathers? For which hath not been sent any authority from God; Wait then, and verily I too, with you be of those who wait.\nفَاَنْجَيْنٰهُ وَالَّذِيْنَ مَعَهٗ بِرَحْمَةٍ مِّنَّا وَ قَطَعْنَا دَابِرَ الَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَمَا كَانُوْا مُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(72)\n\nSo We delivered him and those with him by mercy from us, and We did cut away the roots of those who belied Our signs, and (they) were not believers.\nوَاِلٰى ثَمُوْدَ اَخَاهُمْ صٰلِحًا ۘ قَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اعْبُدُوْا اللّٰهَ مَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ اِلٰهٍ غَيْرُهٗ ؕ قَدْ جَآءَتْكُمْ بَيِّنَةٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ ؕ هٰذِهٖ نَاقَةُ اللّٰهِ لَكُمْ اٰيَةً فَذَرُوْهَا تَاْكُلْ فِىْۤ اَرْضِ اللّٰهِ وَلَا تَمَسُّوْهَا بِسُوْٓءٍ فَيَاْخُذَكُمْ عَذَابٌ اَ لِيْمٌ‏(73)\n\nAnd unto (the people of) Thamud (We did send) their brother Saleh, He said: “O’ my people! Worship ye God (alone) Ye have no god other than Him; Indeed came unto you a clear proof from your Lord; This is the She-camel of God (which) unto you is a Sign, so leave it (free) to pasture in God’s earth and touch her not with any harm, or ye shall be seized with a painful chastisement.\nوَاذْكُرُوْۤا اِذْ جَعَلَكُمْ خُلَفَآءَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ عَادٍ وَّبَوَّاَكُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ تَتَّخِذُوْنَ مِنْ سُهُوْلِهَا قُصُوْرًا وَّتَنْحِتُوْنَ الْجِبَالَ بُيُوْتًا ۚ فَاذْكُرُوْۤا اٰ لَۤاءَ اللّٰهِ وَلَا تَعْثَوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ مُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(74)\n\nAnd remember when He made you successors after the (people) ‘Ad’ and settled you in the earth, ye build mansions on its plain and hew the mountains into dwellings; So remember ye the bounties of God, and seek ye not evil in the earth, making mischief.\nقَالَ الْمَلَاُ الَّذِيْنَ اسْتَكْبَرُوْا مِنْ قَوْمِهٖ لِلَّذِيْنَ اسْتُضْعِفُوْا لِمَنْ اٰمَنَ مِنْهُمْ اَتَعْلَمُوْنَ اَنَّ صٰلِحًا مُّرْسَلٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّهٖؕ قَالُوْۤا اِنَّا بِمَاۤ اُرْسِلَ بِهٖ مُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(75)\n\nSaid the chiefs of those who were puffed up with pride among his people to those who were reckoned weak, to those who believed from among them; “Know ye that Saleh is sent by his Lord?” Said they: “Verily, in what he hath been sent with, we are believers.\nقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ اسْتَكْبَرُوْۤا اِنَّا بِالَّذِىْۤ اٰمَنْتُمْ بِهٖ كٰفِرُوْنَ‏(76)\n\nSaid those who were puffed up with pride; “Verily we, in that which ye believe are disbelievers.\nفَعَقَرُوا النَّاقَةَ وَعَتَوْا عَنْ اَمْرِ رَبِّهِمْ وَ قَالُوْا يٰصٰلِحُ ائْتِنَا بِمَا تَعِدُنَاۤ اِنْ كُنْتَ مِنَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ‏(77)\n\nThey ham-strung the She-Camel and rebelled against the command of their Lord, and they said: “O’ Saleh! Bring us what thou didst threaten us with, if thou art of the apostles.\nفَاَخَذَتْهُمُ الرَّجْفَةُ فَاَصْبَحُوْا فِىْ دَارِهِمْ جٰثِمِيْنَ‏(78)\n\nThen seized them (unawares) the earthquake, so became they in their dwellings, motionless (dead).\nفَتَوَلّٰى عَنْهُمْ وَقَالَ يٰقَوْمِ لَقَدْ اَبْلَغْتُكُمْ رِسَالَةَ رَبِّىْ وَنَصَحْتُ لَكُمْ وَلٰكِنْ لَّا تُحِبُّوْنَ النّٰصِحِيْنَ‏(79)\n\nThen he turned away from them and said: “O’ my people! Indeed I did deliver unto you the message of my Lord, and did admonish you, but ye love not the admonishers.\nوَلُوْطًا اِذْ قَالَ لِقَوْمِهٖۤ اَتَاْتُوْنَ الْفَاحِشَةَ مَا سَبَقَكُمْ بِهَا مِنْ اَحَدٍ مِّنَ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(80)\n\nAnd (We did send) Lot, when said he to his people: “What! Commit ye a lewdness, which did not commit before you, anyone in the worlds?\nاِنَّكُمْ لَتَاْتُوْنَ الرِّجَالَ شَهْوَةً مِّنْ دُوْنِ النِّسَآءِ ؕ بَلْ اَنْتُمْ قَوْمٌ مُّسْرِفُوْنَ‏(81)\n\nVerily ye come to men in lust instead of women; nay, ye are a transgressor people.\nوَمَا كَانَ جَوَابَ قَوْمِهٖۤ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ قَالُوْۤا اَخْرِجُوْهُمْ مِّنْ قَرْيَتِكُمْ ۚ اِنَّهُمْ اُنَاسٌ يَّتَطَهَّرُوْنَ‏(82)\n\nAnd (there) was not any answer of his people except that they said: “Turn ye them out of your town, verily they are a people who seek to purify (themselves).\nفَاَنْجَيْنٰهُ وَاَهْلَهٗۤ اِلَّا امْرَاَتَهٗ ۖ كَانَتْ مِنَ الْغٰبِرِيْنَ‏(83)\n\nSo did We deliver him and his family, except his wife, she was of those who remained behind.\nوَاَمْطَرْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ مَّطَرًا ؕ فَانْظُرْ كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(84)\n\nAnd We rained down on them a shower (of stones); Behold! then, what had been the end of the criminals.\nوَاِلٰى مَدْيَنَ اَخَاهُمْ شُعَيْبًا ؕ قَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ مَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ اِلٰهٍ غَيْرُهٗ ؕ قَدْ جَآءَتْكُمْ بَيِّنَةٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ فَاَوْفُوا الْكَيْلَ وَالْمِيْزَانَ وَلَا تَبْخَسُوا النَّاسَ اَشْيَآءَهُمْ وَلَا تُفْسِدُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ بَعْدَ اِصْلَاحِهَا ؕ ذٰ لِكُمْ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ ۚ‏(85)\n\nAnd unto (the people of) Madyan (We did send) their brother Shu’aib; said he: “O’ my people! worship ye God (alone), ye have no god other than Him; Indeed hath come unto you from your Lord a clear proof, so give ye full measure and weight, and diminish ye not to men their things, and make ye no mischief in the earth, after its reform; This is better for you, if ye be believers.\nوَلَا تَقْعُدُوْا بِكُلِّ صِرَاطٍ تُوْعِدُوْنَ وَتَصُدُّوْنَ عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ مَنْ اٰمَنَ بِهٖ وَتَبْغُوْنَهَا عِوَجًا ۚ وَاذْكُرُوْۤا اِذْ كُنْتُمْ قَلِيْلًا فَكَثَّرَكُمْوَانْظُرُوْا كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الْمُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(86)\n\nAnd sit ye not in every path, threatening and hindering from the path of God, him who believeth in Him, and seeking to make it crooked; And remember ye, when ye were few He multiplied you, and behold ye what had been the end of the mischief-makers.\nوَاِنْ كَانَ طَآئِفَةٌ مِّنْكُمْ اٰمَنُوْا بِالَّذِىْۤ اُرْسِلْتُ بِهٖ وَطَآئِفَةٌ لَّمْ يُؤْمِنُوْا فَاصْبِرُوْا حَتّٰى يَحْكُمَ اللّٰهُ بَيْنَنَا ۚ وَهُوَ خَيْرُ الْحٰكِمِيْنَ‏(87)\n\nAnd if there be a party of you who believe in what I am sent with, and another party who believe not, then wait ye with patience until judgeth God between us; and He is the Best of the judges.\nقَالَ الْمَلَاُ الَّذِيْنَ اسْتَكْبَرُوْا مِنْ قَوْمِهٖ لَنُخْرِجَنَّكَ يٰشُعَيْبُ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مَعَكَ مِنْ قَرْيَتِنَاۤ اَوْ لَتَعُوْدُنَّ فِىْ مِلَّتِنَا ؕ قَالَ اَوَلَوْ كُنَّا كَارِهِيْنَ ۚ‏(88)\n\nSaid the chief of those puffed with pride from among his people: “Certainly we will turn thee out O’ Shu’aib, and those who believe with thee, from our town, or ye shall return into our faith” Said he: “What! Even though we be those who detest (it)?\nقَدِ افْتَرَيْنَا عَلَى اللّٰهِ كَذِبًا اِنْ عُدْنَا فِىْ مِلَّتِكُمْ بَعْدَ اِذْ نَجّٰٮنَا اللّٰهُ مِنْهَا ؕ وَمَا يَكُوْنُ لَنَاۤ اَنْ نَّعُوْدَ فِيْهَاۤ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يَّشَآءَ اللّٰهُ رَبُّنَا ؕ وَسِعَ رَبُّنَا كُلَّ شَىْءٍ عِلْمًاؕ عَلَى اللّٰهِ تَوَكَّلْنَا ؕ رَبَّنَا افْتَحْ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَ قَوْمِنَا بِالْحَقِّ وَاَنْتَ خَيْرُ الْفٰتِحِيْنَ‏(89)\n\nIndeed we shall have forged a lie against God if we return in your faith after when delivered us God from it; it fitteth us not that we return into it, save if it willeth God our Lord; our Lord comprehendeth everything in His knowledge; on God (alone) do we rely; O’ Our Lord! Decide between us and between our people with truth, and Thou art the Best of Deciders.\nوَقَالَ الْمَلَاُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْ قَوْمِهٖ لَئِنِ اتَّبَعْتُمْ شُعَيْبًا اِنَّكُمْ اِذًا لَّخٰسِرُوْنَ‏(90)\n\nAnd said the chiefs of those who disbelieved from among his people: “(Beware!) If ye follow Shu’aib, certainly then ye shall surely be losers.\nفَاَخَذَتْهُمُ الرَّجْفَةُ فَاَصْبَحُوْا فِىْ دَارِهِمْ جٰثِمِيْنَ ۛۙ  ۚ   ۖ‏(91)\n\nThen seized them (unawares) the earthquake, so became they in their dwellings, motionless bodies (dead).\nالَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا شُعَيْبًا كَاَنْ لَّمْ يَغْنَوْا فِيْهَا ۛۚ اَ لَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا شُعَيْبًا كَانُوْا هُمُ الْخٰسِرِيْنَ‏(92)\n\nThose who belied Shu’aib became as if they never dwelt therein; Those who belied Shu’aib (it is) they (who) were the losers.\nفَتَوَلّٰى عَنْهُمْ وَقَالَ يٰقَوْمِ لَقَدْ اَبْلَغْتُكُمْ رِسٰلٰتِ رَبِّىْ وَنَصَحْتُ لَكُمْۚ فَكَيْفَ اٰسٰی عَلٰى قَوْمٍ كٰفِرِيْنَ‏(93)\n\nSo turned he away from them and said he: “O’ Ye people! Indeed I delivered unto you the messages of my Lord, and did admonish unto you; so how then shall I be sorry for a disbelieving people?\nوَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا فِىْ قَرْيَةٍ مِّنْ نَّبِىٍّ اِلَّاۤ اَخَذْنَاۤ اَهْلَهَا بِالْبَاْسَآءِ وَالضَّرَّآءِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَضَّرَّعُوْنَ‏(94)\n\nWe sent not in a town an apostle, but seized We its people, with distress and adversity, that they might humble themselves.\nثُمَّ بَدَّلْنَا مَكَانَ السَّيِّئَةِ الْحَسَنَةَ حَتّٰى عَفَوْا وَّقَالُوْا قَدْ مَسَّ اٰبَآءَنَا الضَّرَّآءُ وَالسَّرَّآءُ فَاَخَذْنٰهُمْ بَغْتَةً وَّهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُوْنَ‏(95)\n\nThen changed We, in the place of evil, good, until they grew multiplied and said they: “Indeed did touch (befall) our fathers (also) adversity and happiness; “We seized them suddenly (by surprise) while they were not aware.\nوَلَوْ اَنَّ اَهْلَ الْقُرٰٓى اٰمَنُوْا وَاتَّقَوْا لَفَتَحْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ بَرَكٰتٍ مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَلٰكِنْ كَذَّبُوْا فَاَخَذْنٰهُمْ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(96)\n\nAnd if the people of the towns had believed and guarded (themselves against evil) We would have opened up for them blessings from the heavens and the earth, but they belied, so We seized them for what they did earn.\nاَفَاَمِنَ اَهْلُ الْقُرٰٓى اَنْ يَّاْتِيَهُمْ بَاْسُنَا بَيَاتًا وَّهُمْ نَآئِمُوْنَؕ‏(97)\n\nWhat! Do the people of the towns then feel secure from coming unto them Our torment by night, while they are asleep?\nاَوَاَمِنَ اَهْلُ الْقُرٰٓى اَنْ يَّاْتِيَهُمْ بَاْسُنَا ضُحًى وَّهُمْ يَلْعَبُوْنَ‏(98)\n\nOr feel secure the people of the towns from coming unto them Our torment in the morning, while they are disporting?\nاَفَاَمِنُوْا مَكْرَ اللّٰهِ ۚ فَلَا يَاْمَنُ مَكْرَ اللّٰهِ اِلَّا الْقَوْمُ الْخٰسِرُوْنَ‏(99)\n\nWhat! Do they then feel secure against the plan of God? But feeleth not secure any one save the people (who are the) losers.\nاَوَلَمْ يَهْدِ لِلَّذِيْنَ يَرِثُوْنَ الْاَرْضَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ اَهْلِهَاۤ اَنْ لَّوْ نَشَآءُ اَصَبْنٰهُمْ بِذُنُوْبِهِمْ ۚ وَنَطْبَعُ عَلٰى قُلُوْبِهِمْ فَهُمْ لَا يَسْمَعُوْنَ‏(100)\n\nIs it not (a lesson) guiding (enough) for those who inherit the earth after its former people that if We please We would afflict (too) for their sins, and set a seal on their hearts that they would not hearken?\nتِلْكَ الْقُرٰى نَقُصُّ عَلَيْكَ مِنْ اَنْۢبَآئِهَا ۚ وَلَقَدْ جَآءَتْهُمْ رُسُلُهُمْ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ ۚ فَمَا كَانُوْا لِيُؤْمِنُوْا بِمَا كَذَّبُوْا مِنْ قَبْلُ ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يَطْبَعُ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى قُلُوْبِ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(101)\n\nThese towns - We relate unto thee (some) of their events, and (that) indeed did come unto them their apostles with clear evidences (miracles), but they would believe not in what they belied from before; Thus doth setteth God a seal on the hearts of the infidels.\nوَمَا وَجَدْنَا لِاَكْثَرِهِمْ مِّنْ عَهْدٍۚ وَاِنْ وَّجَدْنَاۤ اَكْثَرَهُمْ لَفٰسِقِيْنَ‏(102)\n\nWe found not in most of them any (faithfulness to the) covenant, and only found We most of them to be transgressors.\nثُمَّ بَعَثْنَا مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْ مُّوْسٰى بِاٰيٰتِنَاۤ اِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ وَمَلَا۟ئِهٖ فَظَلَمُوْا بِهَا ۚ فَانْظُرْ كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الْمُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(103)\n\nThen raised We, after them Moses with Our signs unto Pharaoh and his chiefs, but they were aggressive with it, see then what was the end of the mischief-makers.\nوَ قَالَ مُوْسٰى يٰفِرْعَوْنُ اِنِّىْ رَسُوْلٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَۙ‏(104)\n\nAnd said Moses: “O’ Pharaoh! Verily I am an apostle from the Lord of the worlds,\nحَقِيْقٌ عَلٰٓى اَنْ لَّاۤ اَقُوْلَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ اِلَّا الْحَقَّ ؕ قَدْ جِئْتُكُمْ بِبَيِّنَةٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ فَاَرْسِلْ مَعِىَ بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ ؕ‏(105)\n\n(It is) incumbent upon (me) that I say not anything about God save the truth; indeed I have brought unto you with clear signs (miracles) from your Lord, so send Thou with me the children of Israel.\nقَالَ اِنْ كُنْتَ جِئْتَ بِاٰيَةٍ فَاْتِ بِهَاۤ اِنْ كُنْتَ مِنَ الصّٰدِقِيْنَ‏(106)\n\nHe said: “If thou hast come with a sign, then bring it, if thou art of the truthful ones.\nفَاَلْقٰى عَصَاهُ فَاِذَا هِىَ ثُعْبَانٌ مُّبِيْنٌ  ۖ ۚ‏(107)\n\nSo he (Moses) threw (down) his rod, and lo! It was a serpent clearly seen.\nوَّنَزَعَ يَدَهٗ فَاِذَا هِىَ بَيْضَآءُ لِلنّٰظِرِيْنَ‏(108)\n\nThen drew he (Moses) forth his hand (out of his bosom) and lo! it was white (shining bright) to (all) beholders.\nقَالَ الْمَلَاُ مِنْ قَوْمِ فِرْعَوْنَ اِنَّ هٰذَا لَسٰحِرٌ عَلِيْمٌ ۙ‏(109)\n\nSaid the chiefs of the people of Pharaoh: “Verily this indeed is an enchanter (most) learned.\nيُّرِيْدُ اَنْ يُّخْرِجَكُمْ مِّنْ اَرْضِكُمْ ۚ فَمَاذَا تَاْمُرُوْنَ‏(110)\n\nHe intendeth to turn you out of your land; What is it then ye counsel?\nقَالُوْآ اَرْجِهْ وَاَخَاہُ وَاَرْسِلْ فِی الْمَدَآئِنِ حٰشِرِیْنَ ۙ‏(111)\n\nSaid they: “Put him off and his brother, and send thou into the cities, collectors,\nيَاْتُوْكَ بِكُلِّ سٰحِرٍ عَلِيْمٍ‏(112)\n\nThat they may (collect and) bring unto thee every enchanter (who is most) learned.\nوَجَآءَ السَّحَرَةُ فِرْعَوْنَ قَالُوْۤا اِنَّ لَنَا لَاَجْرًا اِنْ كُنَّا نَحْنُ الْغٰلِبِيْنَ‏(113)\n\nAnd came the enchanters unto Pharaoh and said they: “Verily for us must be a reward if we be the triumphants.\nقَالَ نَعَمْ وَاِنَّكُمْ لَمِنَ الْمُقَرَّبِيْنَ‏(114)\n\nSaid he: “Yea! (even more) and Verily ye shall certainly be of those nearest (to me).\nقَالُوْا يٰمُوْسٰٓى اِمَّاۤ اَنْ تُلْقِىَ وَاِمَّاۤ اَنْ نَّكُوْنَ نَحْنُ الْمُلْقِيْنَ‏(115)\n\nThey (the enchanters) said: “O’ Moses! Wilt thou cast (thy rod first) or shall We be the (first) casters.\nقَالَ اَلْقُوْا ۚ فَلَمَّاۤ اَلْقَوْا سَحَرُوْۤا اَعْيُنَ النَّاسِ وَاسْتَرْهَبُوْهُمْ وَجَآءُوْ بِسِحْرٍ عَظِيْمٍ‏(116)\n\nSaid he: (Moses) “Cast ye (first)! So when they did cast they bewitched the eyes of the people and terrified them, and produced they a great enchantment.\nوَاَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلٰى مُوْسٰٓى اَنْ اَلْقِ عَصَاكَ ۚ فَاِذَا هِىَ تَلْقَفُ مَا يَاْفِكُوْنَ ۚ‏(117)\n\nAnd revealed We unto Moses saying: “Cast thou thy rod!” then lo! it swallowed (one after another all), that they falsely demonstrated.\nفَوَقَعَ الْحَقُّ وَبَطَلَ مَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَۚ‏(118)\n\nSo was established the truth and was made vain what (all) they were doing\nفَغُلِبُوْا هُنَالِكَ وَانْقَلَبُوْا صٰغِرِيْنَۚ‏(119)\n\nSo (Pharaoh and his enchanters) were defeated on the spot, and returned humbled down.\nوَ اُلْقِىَ السَّحَرَةُ سٰجِدِيْنَ ۙ‏(120)\n\nAnd the enchanters threw (themselves) down prostrating (in adoration)\nقَالُوْۤا اٰمَنَّا بِرَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ ۙ‏(121)\n\nSaid they: “We believe in the Lord of the worlds,\nرَبِّ مُوْسٰى وَهٰرُوْنَ‏(122)\n\nThe Lord of Moses and Aaron.\nقَالَ فِرْعَوْنُ اٰمَنْتُمْ بِهٖ قَبْلَ اَنْ اٰذَنَ لَكُمْۚ اِنَّ هٰذَا لَمَكْرٌ مَّكَرْتُمُوْهُ فِى الْمَدِيْنَةِ لِتُخْرِجُوْا مِنْهَاۤ اَهْلَهَا ۚ فَسَوْفَ تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(123)\n\nSaid Pharaoh: “What? Believe ye in Him ere - I give permission unto you? Verily, this is a plot ye have plotted in the city, that ye may turn out of it its people, but soon ye shall know (the consequences).\nلَاُقَطِّعَنَّ اَيْدِيَكُمْ وَاَرْجُلَكُمْ مِّنْ خِلَافٍ ثُمَّ لَاُصَلِّبَنَّكُمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَ‏(124)\n\nSurely will I cut off your hands and your feet on opposite sides, then will I crucify you all together.\nقَالُوْۤا اِنَّاۤ اِلٰى رَبِّنَا مُنْقَلِبُوْنَۚ‏(125)\n\nSaid they: “Verily unto Our Lord we return.\nوَمَا تَنْقِمُ مِنَّاۤ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ اٰمَنَّا بِاٰيٰتِ رَبِّنَا لَمَّا جَآءَتْنَا ؕ رَبَّنَاۤ اَفْرِغْ عَلَيْنَا صَبْرًا وَّتَوَفَّنَا مُسْلِمِيْنَ‏(126)\n\nAnd thou dost not wreak vengeance on us except because believed we in the signs of our Lord when they came unto us: O’ Our Lord! pour out upon us patience and cause us to die submitting (unto Thee, i.e., as Muslims).\nوَقَالَ الْمَلَاُ مِنْ قَوْمِ فِرْعَوْنَ اَتَذَرُ مُوْسٰى وَقَوْمَهٗ لِيُفْسِدُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَيَذَرَكَ وَاٰلِهَتَكَ ؕ قَالَ سَنُقَتِّلُ اَبْنَآءَهُمْ وَنَسْتَحْىٖ نِسَآءَهُمْ ۚ وَاِنَّا فَوْقَهُمْ قَاهِرُوْنَ‏(127)\n\nAnd said the chiefs of the people of Pharaoh: What! leavest thou Moses and his people to make mischief in the earth and to desert thee and thy gods? Said He: “Soon will we slay their sons and suffer their women alive; Verily we, over them have hold.\nقَالَ مُوْسٰى لِقَوْمِهِ اسْتَعِيْنُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَاصْبِرُوْا ۚ اِنَّ الْاَرْضَ لِلّٰهِ ۙ يُوْرِثُهَا مَنْ يَّشَآءُ مِنْ عِبَادِهٖ ؕ وَالْعَاقِبَةُ لِلْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(128)\n\nMoses said unto his people: “Seek ye help from God and be patient: Verily the earth is God’s, granteth He as heritage unto whomsoever He pleaseth among His servants.” And the end is (only) for those who guard against evil.\nقَالُوْۤا اُوْذِيْنَا مِنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ تَاْتِيَنَا وَمِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا جِئْتَنَا ؕ قَالَ عَسٰى رَبُّكُمْ اَنْ يُّهْلِكَ عَدُوَّكُمْ وَيَسْتَخْلِفَكُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ فَيَنْظُرَ كَيْفَ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(129)\n\nSaid they: “We have been persecuted before camest thou unto us and since thou hath come unto us;” Said he (Moses); “Maybe that your Lord will destroy your enemy and make ye the inheritors in the earth so that He may see how ye act (therein).\nوَلَقَدْ اَخَذْنَاۤ اٰلَ فِرْعَوْنَ بِالسِّنِيْنَ وَنَقْصٍ مِّنَ الثَّمَرٰتِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَذَّكَّرُوْنَ‏(130)\n\nIndeed seized We the people of Pharaoh with (years long) droughts and diminution of fruits that they may be admonished.\nفَاِذَا جَآءَتْهُمُ الْحَسَنَةُ قَالُوْا لَنَا هٰذِهٖ ۚ وَاِنْ تُصِبْهُمْ سَيِّئَةٌ يَّطَّيَّرُوْا بِمُوْسٰى وَمَنْ مَّعَهٗ ؕ اَلَاۤ اِنَّمَا طٰٓئِرُهُمْ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(131)\n\nBut when reached them any good said they “This is due to us;” and when any evil did smite them, they ascribed it to ill-luck due to Moses and those with him; Be it known! Verily their ill-luck is only with God; but most of them know not.\nوَقَالُوْا مَهْمَا تَاْتِنَا بِهٖ مِنْ اٰيَةٍ لِّتَسْحَرَنَا بِهَا ۙ فَمَا نَحْنُ لَكَ بِمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(132)\n\nAnd said they: “Whatever thou mayest bring unto us of any sign to enchant us with it, we will not believe in thee.\nفَاَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمُ الطُّوْفَانَ وَالْجَرَادَ وَالْقُمَّلَ وَالضَّفَادِعَ وَالدَّمَ اٰيٰتٍ مُّفَصَّلٰتٍ فَاسْتَكْبَرُوْا وَكَانُوْا قَوْمًا مُّجْرِمِيْنَ‏(133)\n\nSo We sent upon them widespread calamities, (of wholesale death), and the locust and the lice, and the frogs and the blood, clear signs, yet they behaved proudly and so they were a guilty people.\nوَلَمَّا وَقَعَ عَلَيْهِمُ الرِّجْزُ قَالُوْا يٰمُوْسَى ادْعُ لَنَا رَبَّكَ بِمَا عَهِدَ عِنْدَكَۚ لَئِنْ كَشَفْتَ عَنَّا الرِّجْزَ لَنُؤْمِنَنَّ لَكَ وَلَنُرْسِلَنَّ مَعَكَ بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَۚ‏(134)\n\nAnd whenever fell upon them the torment said they: “O’ Moses! pray unto thy Lord as He covenanted with thee, if thou removeth from us the torment, surely will we believe in thee, and surely will we send with thee the children of Israel.\nفَلَمَّا كَشَفْنَا عَنْهُمُ الرِّجْزَ اِلٰٓى اَجَلٍ هُمْ بٰلِغُوْهُ اِذَا هُمْ يَنْكُثُوْنَ‏(135)\n\nBut whenever removed We the torment from them till a fixed term which they should reach, lo! they broke (their promise).\nفَانْتَقَمْنَا مِنْهُمْ فَاَغْرَقْنٰهُمْ فِى الْيَمِّ بِاَنَّهُمْ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَكَانُوْا عَنْهَا غٰفِلِيْنَ‏(136)\n\nSo We did inflict retribution on them, and drowned them in the sea, because they belied Our signs and were heedless of them.\nوَاَوْرَثْنَا الْقَوْمَ الَّذِيْنَ كَانُوْا يُسْتَضْعَفُوْنَ مَشَارِقَ الْاَرْضِ وَمَغَارِبَهَا الَّتِىْ بٰرَكْنَا فِيْهَا ؕ وَتَمَّتْ كَلِمَتُ رَبِّكَ الْحُسْنٰى عَلٰى بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَاۤءِيْلَۙ بِمَا صَبَرُوْا ؕ وَدَمَّرْنَا مَا كَانَ يَصْنَعُ فِرْعَوْنُ وَقَوْمُهٗ وَمَا كَانُوْا يَعْرِشُوْنَ‏(137)\n\nAnd made We inheritors the people who were deemed weak (to inherit) the eastern parts of the earth and the western parts of it, which we had blessed therein (with fertility); and the good word of thy Lord was fulfilled in the children of Israel for what they did endure; and destroyed We, what Pharaoh and his people had wrought, and what shade they did make.\nوَجَاوَزْنَا بِبَنِىْۤ اِسْرَاۤءِيْلَ الْبَحْرَ فَاَ تَوْا عَلٰى قَوْمٍ يَّعْكُفُوْنَ عَلٰٓى اَصْنَامٍ لَّهُمْ ۚ قَالُوْا يٰمُوْسَى اجْعَلْ لَّنَاۤ اِلٰهًا كَمَا لَهُمْ اٰلِهَةٌ  ؕ قَالَ اِنَّكُمْ قَوْمٌ تَجْهَلُوْنَ‏(138)\n\nAnd We caused the children of Israel to cross (safely) the sea, then they came upon a people devoted (themselves) to the worship of the idols of their own; said they (the children of Israel): “O’ Moses! Make thou for us a god as they have gods of their own. Said he, “Verily ye are a people behaving ignorantly.\nاِنَّ هٰٓؤُلَۤاءِ مُتَبَّرٌ مَّا هُمْ فِيْهِ وَبٰطِلٌ مَّا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(139)\n\nAs to these people, surely in what they are, shall be destroyed, and vain it is what they do.\nقَالَ اَغَيْرَ اللّٰهِ اَبْغِيْكُمْ اِلٰهًا وَّهُوَ فَضَّلَكُمْ عَلَى الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(140)\n\n(And) said he: “What! Other than (the true) God, shall I seek for you a god, while He hath exalted you over (the people of the) worlds?\nوَاِذْ اَنْجَيْنٰكُمْ مِّنْ اٰلِ فِرْعَوْنَ يَسُوْمُوْنَكُمْ سُوْٓءَ الْعَذَابِ ۚ يُقَتِّلُوْنَ اَبْنَآءَكُمْ وَ يَسْتَحْيُوْنَ نِسَآءَكُمْ ؕ وَفِىْ ذٰ لِكُمْ بَلَاۤ ءٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ عَظِيْمٌ‏(141)\n\nAnd (remember ye) when We rescued you, from the people of Pharaoh, who afflicted you with grievous torment, slaying your sons and leaving alive your women, and in this, for you was a great trial from your Lord.\nوَوٰعَدْنَا مُوْسٰى ثَلٰثِيْنَ لَيْلَةً وَّاَتْمَمْنٰهَا بِعَشْرٍ فَتَمَّ مِيْقَاتُ رَبِّهٖۤ اَرْبَعِيْنَ لَيْلَةً  ۚ وَقَالَ مُوْسٰى لِاَخِيْهِ هٰرُوْنَ اخْلُفْنِىْ فِىْ قَوْمِىْ وَاَصْلِحْ وَلَا تَتَّبِعْ سَبِيْلَ الْمُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(142)\n\nAnd We made appointment with Moses for thirty nights and completed it with ten (more), Thus was completed the term of his Lord forty nights, and (before he went up) said Moses unto his brother Aaron: “Take thou my place among my people, Act rightly and follow not the path of the mischief-makers\nوَلَمَّا جَآءَ مُوْسٰى لِمِيْقَاتِنَا وَكَلَّمَهٗ رَبُّهٗ ۙ قَالَ رَبِّ اَرِنِىْۤ اَنْظُرْ اِلَيْكَ ؕ قَالَ لَنْ تَرٰٮنِىْ وَلٰكِنِ انْظُرْ اِلَى الْجَبَلِ فَاِنِ اسْتَقَرَّ مَكَانَهٗ فَسَوْفَ تَرٰٮنِىْ ۚ فَلَمَّا تَجَلّٰى رَبُّهٗ لِلْجَبَلِ جَعَلَهٗ دَكًّا وَّخَرَّ مُوْسٰى صَعِقًا ۚ فَلَمَّاۤ اَفَاقَ قَالَ سُبْحٰنَكَ تُبْتُ اِلَيْكَ وَاَنَا اَوَّلُ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(143)\n\nAnd when came Moses at Our appointment and spake unto him his Lord, said: he “O’ My Lord! Show (Thyself) unto me, that I may look towards Thee;” He (God) said: (O’ Moses!) never shalt thou see me, but look towards the mountain, if it remaineth firm in its place, then soon wilt thou see me, but when his Lord did manifest His glory unto the mountain, He made it crumble, and fell Moses down senseless: and when he recovered (his senses) said he: “Glory be to Thee (O’ My Lord!) I turn unto Thee (repentant) I am the first of the believers.\nقَالَ يٰمُوْسٰٓى اِنِّى اصْطَفَيْتُكَ عَلَى النَّاسِ بِرِسٰلٰتِىْ وَ بِكَلَامِىْ ۖ  فَخُذْ مَاۤ اٰتَيْتُكَ وَكُنْ مِّنَ الشّٰكِرِيْنَ‏(144)\n\nHe said: “O’ Moses! Verily I have chosen thee above the people with My messages and with My words (discourse); take then what I give thee and be thou of the grateful ones.\nوَكَتَبْنَا لَهٗ فِى الْاَلْوَاحِ مِنْ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ مَّوْعِظَةً وَّتَفْصِيْلًا لِّكُلِّ شَىْءٍ ۚ فَخُذْهَا بِقُوَّةٍ وَّاْمُرْ قَوْمَكَ يَاْخُذُوْا بِاَحْسَنِهَا ؕ سَاُورِيْكُمْ دَارَ الْفٰسِقِيْنَ‏(145)\n\nAnd wrote We for him, in the Tablets lessons of every kind and explanation of every thing; and (said unto Moses): “Hold thou these with firmness and bid thy people to hold fast what is best thereof; Soon will I show you the abode of the wicked.\nسَاَصْرِفُ عَنْ اٰيٰتِىَ الَّذِيْنَ يَتَكَبَّرُوْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ بِغَيْرِ الْحَقِّ ؕ وَاِنْ يَّرَوْا كُلَّ اٰيَةٍ لَّا يُؤْمِنُوْا بِهَا ۚ وَاِنْ يَّرَوْا سَبِيْلَ الرُّشْدِ لَا يَتَّخِذُوْهُ سَبِيْلًا ۚ وَّاِنْ يَّرَوْا سَبِيْلَ الْغَىِّ يَتَّخِذُوْهُ سَبِيْلًا ؕ ذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّهُمْ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَكَانُوْا عَنْهَا غٰفِلِيْنَ‏(146)\n\nSoon will I (allow to) turn away from my signs those (who) unjustly pride in the earth; while (even) if they see all the signs they will not believe in it; and (even) if they see the right way, they will not adopt it for a way; And if they see the way of error, they will adopt it for a way; this is because they belied Our signs and were heedless of them.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَلِقَآءِ الْاٰخِرَةِ حَبِطَتْ اَعْمَالُهُمْؕ هَلْ يُجْزَوْنَ اِلَّا مَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(147)\n\nAnd those who belie Our signs and the meeting of the hereafter, vain shall be their (good) deeds; shall they be recompensed save for what they have wrought?\nوَاتَّخَذَ قَوْمُ مُوْسٰى مِنْۢ بَعْدِهٖ مِنْ حُلِيِّهِمْ عِجْلًا جَسَدًا لَّهٗ خُوَارٌ ؕ اَلَمْ يَرَوْا اَنَّهٗ لَا يُكَلِّمُهُمْ وَلَا يَهْدِيْهِمْ سَبِيْلًا ۘ اِتَّخَذُوْهُ وَكَانُوْا ظٰلِمِيْنَ‏(148)\n\nThe people of Moses after him (in his absence) made of their ornaments, a calf, a (mere) body which seemed to low; Could they see not, it neither speaketh to them, and nor it guideth them in the way? They adopted it (for worship) and they were unjust.\nوَلَمَّا سُقِطَ فِىْۤ اَيْدِيْهِمْ وَرَاَوْا اَنَّهُمْ قَدْ ضَلُّوْا ۙ قَالُوْا لَئِنْ لَّمْ يَرْحَمْنَا رَبُّنَا وَيَغْفِرْ لَنَا لَنَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الْخٰسِرِيْنَ‏(149)\n\nAnd when they repented and saw that they had gone astray, said they: “If Our Lord be not merciful unto us and forgive us (not), surely we shall be of the losers.\nوَلَمَّا رَجَعَ مُوْسٰٓى اِلٰى قَوْمِهٖ غَضْبَانَ اَسِفًا ۙ قَالَ بِئْسَمَا خَلَفْتُمُوْنِىْ مِنْۢ بَعْدِىْ ۚ اَعَجِلْتُمْ اَمْرَ رَبِّكُمْ ۚ وَاَلْقَى الْاَلْوَاحَ وَاَخَذَ بِرَاْسِ اَخِيْهِ يَجُرُّهٗۤ اِلَيْهِؕ قَالَ ابْنَ اُمَّ اِنَّ الْقَوْمَ اسْتَضْعَفُوْنِىْ وَكَادُوْا يَقْتُلُوْنَنِىْ ۖ  فَلَا تُشْمِتْ بِىَ الْاَعْدَآءَ وَ لَا تَجْعَلْنِىْ مَعَ الْقَوْمِ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(150)\n\nAnd when returned Moses unto his people, wrathful and grieved, said he: “evil is it that ye have neglected me; after me ye did make haste about the matter of your Lord?” and he threw down the tablets and seized his brother (Aaron) by the head, dragging him unto him; Said he (Aaron): “O’ Son of my mother! verily the people did reckon me weak and had well-nigh slain me, so make not (my) enemies rejoice over me, and count thou not me among the unjust people.\nقَالَ رَبِّ اغْفِرْ لِىْ وَلِاَخِىْ وَ اَدْخِلْنَا فِىْ رَحْمَتِكَ ۖ  وَاَنْتَ اَرْحَمُ الرّٰحِمِيْنَ‏(151)\n\nSaid he (Moses) (praying) “O’ My Lord! Forgive me and my Brother and admit us into Thy mercy, and Thou art the Most Merciful of the merciful ones.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اتَّخَذُوا الْعِجْلَ سَيَنَالُهُمْ غَضَبٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّهِمْ وَذِلَّةٌ فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا ؕ وَكَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِىْ الْمُفْتَرِيْنَ‏(152)\n\nVerily those who adopted the calf (for a god) soon shall reach them a wrath from their Lord and an indignation in the life of (this) world; and thus do We recompense the forgers of lies.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ عَمِلُوا السَّيِّاٰتِ ثُمَّ تَابُوْا مِنْۢ بَعْدِهَا وَاٰمَنُوْۤا اِنَّ رَبَّكَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهَا لَغَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(153)\n\nAnd those who do evil deeds, then repent they after that, while (in fact) believed Verily thy Lord after that is certainly Oft-Forgiving, Merciful.\nوَلَمَّا سَكَتَ عَنْ مُّوْسَى الْغَضَبُ اَخَذَ الْاَلْوَاحَ ۖ  وَفِىْ نُسْخَتِهَا هُدًى وَّرَحْمَةٌ لِّلَّذِيْنَ هُمْ لِرَبِّهِمْ يَرْهَبُوْنَ‏(154)\n\nAnd when was appeased Moses’ anger, he took up the Tablets and, in the writings therein was guidance and mercy for those who fear for the sake of their Lord.\nوَاخْتَارَ مُوْسٰى قَوْمَهٗ سَبْعِيْنَ رَجُلًا لِّمِيْقَاتِنَا ۚ فَلَمَّاۤ اَخَذَتْهُمُ الرَّجْفَةُ قَالَ رَبِّ لَوْ شِئْتَ اَهْلَكْتَهُمْ مِّنْ قَبْلُ وَاِيَّاىَ ؕ اَ تُهْلِكُنَا بِمَا فَعَلَ السُّفَهَآءُ مِنَّا ۚ اِنْ هِىَ اِلَّا فِتْنَتُكَ ؕ تُضِلُّ بِهَا مَنْ تَشَآءُ وَتَهْدِىْ مَنْ تَشَآءُ ؕ اَنْتَ وَلِيُّنَا فَاغْفِرْ لَنَا وَارْحَمْنَا وَاَنْتَ خَيْرُ الْغَافِرِيْنَ‏(155)\n\nAnd chose Moses, of his people seventy men for Our appointment, then when seized them a shocking, prayed he: “O’ My Lord! Hadst Thou pleased Thou hadst destroyed them and me (too) before; wouldst Thou destroy us for what have done the fools among us? it is naught but Thy trial; Thou causeth whosoever Thou willest to stray and guideth whomsoever Thou pleaseth; Thou art our Guardian, so forgive us and bestow Thy mercy upon us, and Thou art the Best of the forgivers.\nوَاكْتُبْ لَنَا فِىْ هٰذِهِ الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةً وَّفِى الْاٰخِرَةِ اِنَّا هُدْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ ؕ قَالَ عَذَابِىْۤ اُصِيْبُ بِهٖ مَنْ اَشَآءُ ۚ وَرَحْمَتِىْ وَسِعَتْ كُلَّ شَىْءٍ ؕ فَسَاَكْتُبُهَا لِلَّذِيْنَ يَتَّقُوْنَ وَيُؤْتُوْنَ الزَّكٰوةَ وَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ بِاٰيٰتِنَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ ۚ‏(156)\n\nAnd ordain Thou for us good in this world and in the hereafter; (for) Verily we turn unto Thee;” Said He “My chastisement, will I afflict with it, whomsoever I will and My mercy embraceth unto all things, therefore soon will I ordain it (particularly) for those who guard (against evil) and pay the poor-rate, and those who believe in Our signs.\nاَ لَّذِيْنَ يَتَّبِعُوْنَ الرَّسُوْلَ النَّبِىَّ الْاُمِّىَّ الَّذِىْ يَجِدُوْنَهٗ مَكْتُوْبًا عِنْدَهُمْ فِى التَّوْرٰٮةِ وَالْاِنْجِيْلِ يَاْمُرُهُمْ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ وَيَنْهٰٮهُمْ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ وَيُحِلُّ لَهُمُ الطَّيِّبٰتِ وَيُحَرِّمُ عَلَيْهِمُ الْخَبٰۤئِثَ وَيَضَعُ عَنْهُمْ اِصْرَهُمْ وَالْاَغْلٰلَ الَّتِىْ كَانَتْ عَلَيْهِمْ ؕ فَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا بِهٖ وَعَزَّرُوْهُ وَنَصَرُوْهُ وَ اتَّبَعُوا النُّوْرَ الَّذِىْۤ اُنْزِلَ مَعَهٗ ۤ ۙ اُولٰۤئِكَ هُمُ الْمُفْلِحُوْنَ‏(157)\n\nThose who follow the Apostle, Prophet the ‘Ummi’ whom find they, written (in their own scriptures) with them, in the Law and the Evangel; commandeth he unto them (what is) good and he preventeth them from evil, and maketh he lawful unto them the good things, and he prohibiteth unto them the bad (impure) ones, and he removeth from them their burden and the yokes which were upon them; so those who believe in him, and honour him, and help him, and follow the Light which hath been sent down with him, These are they who are the successful ones.\nقُلْ يٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ اِنِّىْ رَسُوْلُ اللّٰهِ اِلَيْكُمْ جَمِيْعَاْ ۨالَّذِىْ لَهٗ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِۚ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ يُحْىٖ وَيُمِيْتُ فَاٰمِنُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهِ النَّبِىِّ الْاُمِّىِّ الَّذِىْ يُؤْمِنُ بِاللّٰهِ وَكَلِمٰتِهٖ وَاتَّبِعُوْهُ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَهْتَدُوْنَ‏(158)\n\nSay (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “O’ ye people, Verily I am the apostle of God unto you all, of Him unto Whom belongeth the kingdom of the heavens and the earth; No god is there but He. He giveth life and causeth death, so believe ye in God and His Apostle, Prophet, the ‘Ummi’ who believeth in God and His Words, So ye follow him that ye may be guided aright.\nوَ مِنْ قَوْمِ مُوْسٰٓى اُمَّةٌ يَّهْدُوْنَ بِالْحَقِّ وَبِهٖ يَعْدِلُوْنَ‏(159)\n\nAnd of Moses’ people is a party who guide (people) with the Truth and thereby do justice.\nوَقَطَّعْنٰهُمُ اثْنَتَىْ عَشْرَةَ اَسْبَاطًا اُمَمًا ؕ وَاَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلٰى مُوْسٰٓى اِذِ اسْتَسْقٰٮهُ قَوْمُهٗۤ اَنِ اضْرِبْ بِّعَصَاكَ الْحَجَرَ ۚ فَاْنۢبَجَسَتْ مِنْهُ اثْنَتَا عَشْرَةَ عَيْنًا ؕ قَدْ عَلِمَ كُلُّ اُنَاسٍ مَّشْرَبَهُمْؕ وَظَلَّلْنَا عَلَيْهِمُ الْغَمَامَ وَاَنْزَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمُ الْمَنَّ وَالسَّلْوٰىؕ كُلُوْا مِنْ طَيِّبٰتِ مَا رَزَقْنٰكُمْؕ وَ مَا ظَلَمُوْنَا وَلٰكِنْ كَانُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ يَظْلِمُوْنَ‏(160)\n\nAnd We divided them into twelve tribes (or) nations; and revealed We unto Moses, when asked him, his people for water: “Strike thou, with thy rod, the rock:” so gushed forth out of it twelve springs; each tribe knew its drinking place; and We caused the clouds to shadow over them, and We sent down unto them manna and quails; (saying) “Eat ye of the good things which We have provided you with”; And they (rebelled and) did no harm unto Us but they unto their own selves were doing injustice.\nوَاِذْ قِيْلَ لَهُمُ اسْكُنُوْا هٰذِهِ الْقَرْيَةَ وَكُلُوْا مِنْهَا حَيْثُ شِئْتُمْ وَقُوْلُوْا حِطَّةٌ وَّادْخُلُوا الْبَابَ سُجَّدًا نَّغْفِرْ لَكُمْ خَطِيْٓئٰتِكُمْ ؕ سَنَزِيْدُ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(161)\n\nAnd when it was said unto them; “Dwell ye in this town and eat ye thereof as ye wish”, and say: “Put down from us our burden (of sins)’’’ and enter ye the gates making obeisance, We will forgive you, your faults; Soon will We give more to the doers of good to others.\nفَبَدَّلَ الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا مِنْهُمْ قَوْلًا غَيْرَ الَّذِىْ قِيْلَ لَهُمْ فَاَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ رِجْزًا مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَظْلِمُوْنَ‏(162)\n\nBut changed those who did injustice among them a word other than that which was spoken unto them, so We did send upon them a pestilence from heaven for they had been doing injustice.\nوَسْئَلْهُمْ عَنِ الْقَرْيَةِ الَّتِىْ كَانَتْ حَاضِرَةَ الْبَحْرِۘ اِذْ يَعْدُوْنَ فِى السَّبْتِ اِذْ تَاْتِيْهِمْ حِيْتَانُهُمْ يَوْمَ سَبْتِهِمْ شُرَّعًا وَّيَوْمَ لَا يَسْبِتُوْنَ ۙ لَا تَاْتِيْهِمْ ۛۚ كَذٰلِكَ ۛۚ نَبْلُوْهُمْ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَفْسُقُوْنَ‏(163)\n\nAnd (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) ask them about the town which was beside the sea; when they did exceed (the limits) in the Sabbath when their fish did come unto them on the day of their Sabbath, appearing on the surface of the water; and on the day they observed not the Sabbath, they (the fish) did not come unto them; Thus did We try them for they were transgressing.\nوَاِذْ قَالَتْ اُمَّةٌ مِّنْهُمْ لِمَ تَعِظُوْنَ قَوْمَاْ  ۙ اۨللّٰهُ مُهْلِكُهُمْ اَوْ مُعَذِّبُهُمْ عَذَابًا شَدِيْدًا ؕ قَالُوْا مَعْذِرَةً اِلٰى رَبِّكُمْ وَلَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَّقُوْنَ‏(164)\n\nAnd when a party of them said: “Why admonish ye a people whom God would destroy or whom He would chastise with a severe chastisement?” said they “To be free from blame before your Lord, perchance they may guard (themselves against evil).\nفَلَمَّا نَسُوْا مَا ذُكِّرُوْا بِهٖۤ اَنْجَيْنَا الَّذِيْنَ يَنْهَوْنَ عَنِ السُّوْۤءِ وَاَخَذْنَا الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا بِعَذَابٍۭ بَئِيْسٍۭ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَفْسُقُوْنَ‏(165)\n\nSo when they did forget what they were warned with, We delivered those who forbade evil and seized those who were unjust with a dreadful chastisement because they were transgressing.\nفَلَمَّا عَتَوْا عَنْ مَّا نُهُوْا عَنْهُ قُلْنَا لَهُمْ كُوْنُوْا قِرَدَةً خٰسِئِیْنَ‏(166)\n\nSo when they proudly defied what they had been forbidden, We said unto them; “Be ye apes despised, spurned (away from the human society).\nوَاِذْ تَاَذَّنَ رَبُّكَ لَيَبْعَثَنَّ عَلَيْهِمْ اِلٰى يَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ مَنْ يَّسُوْمُهُمْ سُوْٓءَ الْعَذَابِ ؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَسَرِيْعُ الْعِقَابِ  ۖۚ وَاِنَّهٗ لَغَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(167)\n\nAnd (recollect O’ Our Apostle!) when declared thy Lord that He would surely send against them until the day of resurrection those who would afflict them with a grievous torment; Verily thy Lord is certainly quick to requite (evil) and Verily He is the Oft-Forgiving and the Most Merciful.\nوَقَطَّعْنٰهُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ اُمَمًا ۚ مِنْهُمُ الصّٰلِحُوْنَ وَمِنْهُمْ دُوْنَ ذٰ لِكَ وَبَلَوْنٰهُمْ بِالْحَسَنٰتِ وَالسَّيِّاٰتِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَرْجِعُوْنَ‏(168)\n\nAnd We did cut (scattered) them in the earth into (different) peoples; of them (some) are righteous, and of them (some) are otherwise, and We did try them with good (The blessings) and (also with) evil that they might return (to the Right path).\nفَخَلَفَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْ خَلْفٌ وَّرِثُوا الْكِتٰبَ يَاْخُذُوْنَ عَرَضَ هٰذَا الْاَدْنٰى وَيَقُوْلُوْنَ سَيُغْفَرُ لَنَا ۚ وَاِنْ يَّاْتِهِمْ عَرَضٌ مِّثْلُهٗ يَاْخُذُوْهُ ؕ اَلَمْ يُؤْخَذْ عَلَيْهِمْ مِّيْثَاقُ الْكِتٰبِ اَنْ لَّا يَقُوْلُوْا عَلَى اللّٰهِ اِلَّا الْحَقَّ وَدَرَسُوْا مَا فِيْهِ ؕ وَالدَّارُ الْاٰخِرَةُ خَيْرٌ لِّلَّذِيْنَ يَتَّقُوْنَ ؕ اَفَلَا تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(169)\n\nThen succeeded after them (an evil) posterity who inherited the Book, taking the goods of this low life saying: “It will be forgiven us;” And if come unto them the like goods they would seize it (too); Was not a covenant of the Book (of Law) taken from them that they would speak not about God save the truth, and (that) they have read what is in it; the abode of the hereafter is the best for those who guard (against evil); What! do ye not then understand?\nوَالَّذِيْنَ يُمَسِّكُوْنَ بِالْكِتٰبِ وَاَقَامُوا الصَّلٰوةَ ؕ اِنَّا لَا نُضِيْعُ اَجْرَ الْمُصْلِحِيْنَ‏(170)\n\nAnd those who hold fast by the Book and establish prayer; verily We waste not the recompense of those who amend (themselves).\nوَاِذْ نَتَقْنَا الْجَبَلَ فَوْقَهُمْ كَاَنَّهٗ ظُلَّةٌ وَّظَنُّوْۤا اَنَّهٗ وَاقِعٌ ۢ بِهِمْ ۚ خُذُوْا مَاۤ اٰتَيْنٰكُمْ بِقُوَّةٍ وَّاذْكُرُوْا مَا فِيْهِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَّقُوْنَ‏(171)\n\nAnd when We shook the Mountain over them as if it were a covering, and thought they that it was going to fall down upon them; (Said We) “Hold ye firmly what We give you and be mindful of what is (there) in it, that ye may guard (yourself against evil).\nوَ اِذْ اَخَذَ رَبُّكَ مِنْۢ بَنِىْۤ اٰدَمَ مِنْ ظُهُوْرِهِمْ ذُرِّيَّتَهُمْ وَ اَشْهَدَهُمْ عَلٰٓى اَنْفُسِهِمْ ۚ اَلَسْتُ بِرَبِّكُمْ ؕ قَالُوْا بَلٰى ۛۚ شَهِدْنَا ۛۚ اَنْ تَقُوْلُوْا يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ اِنَّا كُنَّا عَنْ هٰذَا غٰفِلِيْنَ ۙ‏(172)\n\nWhen brought forth thy Lord from the children of Adam, from their backs, their descendants and (when) made them bear witness upon their own selves (saying): “Am I not your Lord?” replied they “Yea! We do bear witness.” (This We did) lest ye should say on the Day of Judgment “Verily we were of this (fact) unaware.\nاَوْ تَقُوْلُوْۤا اِنَّمَاۤ اَشْرَكَ اٰبَآؤُنَا مِنْ قَبْلُ وَكُنَّا ذُرِّيَّةً مِّنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْۚ اَفَتُهْلِكُنَا بِمَا فَعَلَ الْمُبْطِلُوْنَ‏(173)\n\nOr lest ye should say: “Verily associated (with God) only our fathers from before (us) and we are their descendants after them (following them): wilt Thou then destroy us for what the vain doers did?\nوَكَذٰلِكَ نُفَصِّلُ الْاٰيٰتِ وَلَعَلَّهُمْ يَرْجِعُوْنَ‏(174)\n\nAnd thus do We explain the signs in details and that ye might return (from the error).\nوَاتْلُ عَلَيْهِمْ نَبَاَ الَّذِىْۤ اٰتَيْنٰهُ اٰيٰتِنَا فَانْسَلَخَ مِنْهَا فَاَتْبَعَهُ الشَّيْطٰنُ فَكَانَ مِنَ الْغٰوِيْنَ‏(175)\n\nRelate unto them the news of him whom We gave Our signs, but he withdrew (himself) from them, so Satan followed him; so he was one of those who went astray.\nوَلَوْ شِئْنَا لَرَفَعْنٰهُ بِهَا وَلٰكِنَّهٗۤ اَخْلَدَ اِلَى الْاَرْضِ وَاتَّبَعَ هَوٰٮهُ ۚ فَمَثَلُهٗ كَمَثَلِ الْكَلْبِ ۚ اِنْ تَحْمِلْ عَلَيْهِ يَلْهَثْ اَوْ تَتْرُكْهُ يَلْهَث ؕ ذٰ لِكَ مَثَلُ الْقَوْمِ الَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا ۚ فَاقْصُصِ الْقَصَصَ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَفَكَّرُوْنَ‏(176)\n\nAnd had We willed, We would certainly have exalted him thereby, but he inclined towards the earth and followed his vain inclinations, so his similitude is like the parable of a dog, if thou attacketh him he lolleth out his tongue, or leaveth him alone he lolleth out his tongue; such is the similitude of the people who belie Our signs, so relate (unto them) the stories, that they may reflect.\nسَآءَ مَثَلَاْ ۨالْقَوْمُ الَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَاَنْفُسَهُمْ كَانُوْا يَظْلِمُوْنَ‏(177)\n\nHow evil is the similitude of the people who belie Our signs and unto their own selves they are unjust.\nمَنْ يَّهْدِ اللّٰهُ فَهُوَ الْمُهْتَدِىْۚ وَمَنْ يُّضْلِلْ فَاُولٰۤئِكَ هُمُ الْخٰسِرُوْنَ‏(178)\n\nWhomsoever God doth guide He is the one who is guided aright, and whomsoever He suffereth to stray, these are they the losers.\nوَلَقَدْ ذَرَاْنَا لِجَهَنَّمَ كَثِيْرًا مِّنَ الْجِنِّ وَالْاِنْسِ ۖ  لَهُمْ قُلُوْبٌ لَّا يَفْقَهُوْنَ بِهَا  وَلَهُمْ اَعْيُنٌ لَّا يُبْصِرُوْنَ بِهَا  وَلَهُمْ اٰذَانٌ لَّا يَسْمَعُوْنَ بِهَا ؕ اُولٰۤئِكَ كَالْاَنْعَامِ بَلْ هُمْ اَضَلُّ ؕ اُولٰۤئِكَ هُمُ الْغٰفِلُوْنَ‏(179)\n\nIndeed We have created for hell many of the jinn and the men; They have hearts (but) they understand not with it; and they have eyes (but) they see not with it; and they have ears (but) they hear not with it; they are like cattle, nay, more astray; These are they the heedless ones.\nوَلِلّٰهِ الْاَسْمَآءُ الْحُسْنٰى فَادْعُوْهُ بِهَا وَذَرُوا الَّذِيْنَ يُلْحِدُوْنَ فِىْۤ اَسْمَآئِهٖ ؕ سَيُجْزَوْنَ مَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(180)\n\nAnd to God (alone) belong (all) the most beautiful names, so call on Him thereby, and leave alone those who use profanity in His names; soon shall they be recompensed for what they were doing.\nوَمِمَّنْ خَلَقْنَاۤ اُمَّةٌ يَّهْدُوْنَ بِالْحَقِّ وَبِهٖ يَعْدِلُوْنَ‏(181)\n\nAnd of those whom We did create are a people who guide (others) with truth and themselves justly adhere to it.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا سَنَسْتَدْرِجُهُمْ مِّنْ حَيْثُ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ ۖ  ۚ‏(182)\n\nAnd those who belie Our signs, soon shall We gradually draw them to ruin from whence they know not.\nوَاُمْلِىْ لَهُمْ ؕ اِنَّ كَيْدِىْ مَتِيْنٌ‏(183)\n\nAnd I grant them; respite. Verily My scheme is (unfailingly) strong.\nاَوَلَمْ يَتَفَكَّرُوْا مَا بِصَاحِبِهِمْ مِّنْ جِنَّةٍؕ اِنْ هُوَ اِلَّا نَذِيْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(184)\n\nWhat! reflect they not that their companion (Our Apostle Muhammad) is not seized with madness, He is but only a plain Warner.\nاَوَلَمْ يَنْظُرُوْا فِىْ مَلَكُوْتِ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَمَا خَلَقَ اللّٰهُ مِنْ شَىْءٍ ۙ وَّاَنْ عَسٰٓى اَنْ يَّكُوْنَ قَدِ اقْتَرَبَ اَجَلُهُمْ ۚ فَبِاَىِّ حَدِيْثٍۢ بَعْدَهٗ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(185)\n\nOr look they not into the kingdoms of the heavens and the earth and whatever things (God) created, and maybe that their term hath drawn nigh; then in what other words after this would they believe?\nمَنْ يُّضْلِلِ اللّٰهُ فَلَا هَادِىَ لَهٗ ؕ وَ يَذَرُهُمْ فِىْ طُغْيَانِهِمْ يَعْمَهُوْنَ‏(186)\n\nWhomsoever God suffereth to stray there is no guide for him, and He leaveth them alone in their transgression, blindly wandering (bewildered).\nيَسْئَلُوْنَكَ عَنِ السَّاعَةِ اَيَّانَ مُرْسٰٮهَا ؕ قُلْ اِنَّمَا عِلْمُهَا عِنْدَ رَبِّىْ ۚ لَا يُجَلِّيْهَا لِوَقْتِهَاۤ اِلَّا هُوَۘ ؕ ثَقُلَتْ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ لَا تَاْتِيْكُمْ اِلَّا بَغْتَةً  ؕ يَسْئَلُوْنَكَ كَاَنَّكَ حَفِىٌّ عَنْهَا ؕ قُلْ اِنَّمَا عِلْمُهَا عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(187)\n\nThey ask thee about the Hour (of Resurrection) when will be its fixed time; Say: “The knowledge of it is only with my Lord, None shall manifest it at its time but He; Heavy shall it be in the heavens and the earth; it will not come to you but of a sudden.” They ask thee as if thou wert solicitous about it. Say: “Its knowledge is only with God, but most people know not.\nقُلْ لَّاۤ اَمْلِكُ لِنَفْسِىْ نَفْعًا وَّلَا ضَرًّا اِلَّا مَا شَآءَ اللّٰهُ ؕ وَلَوْ كُنْتُ اَعْلَمُ الْغَيْبَ لَاسْتَكْثَرْتُ مِنَ الْخَيْرِ ۖ ۛۚ وَمَا مَسَّنِىَ السُّۤوْءُ ۛۚ اِنْ اَنَا اِلَّا نَذِيْرٌ وَّبَشِيْرٌ لِّقَوْمٍ يُّؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(188)\n\nSay: ‘neither I own for myself any benefit nor harm except what willeth God; and had I known the unseen indeed I would have had much of good and evil had touched me not, and I am not but a Warner and the bearer of good news for a people who believe?\nهُوَ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَكُمْ مِّنْ نَّفْسٍ وَّاحِدَةٍ وَّجَعَلَ مِنْهَا زَوْجَهَا لِيَسْكُنَ اِلَيْهَا ۚ فَلَمَّا تَغَشّٰٮهَا حَمَلَتْ حَمْلًا خَفِيْفًا فَمَرَّتْ بِهٖ ۚ فَلَمَّاۤ اَثْقَلَتْ دَّعَوَا اللّٰهَ رَبَّهُمَا لَئِنْ اٰتَيْتَنَا صَالِحًا لَّنَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الشّٰكِرِيْنَ‏(189)\n\nHe it is who created you from a single self and from it did He make his mate that he may dwell resting unto her, when he covereth her, she beareth a light burden and carrieth it, when it groweth more heavy they both pray to their Lord; ‘‘If Thou givest us a good child, certainly we shall be of the grateful ones.\nفَلَمَّاۤ اٰتٰٮهُمَا صَالِحًا جَعَلَا لَهٗ شُرَكَآءَ فِيْمَاۤ اٰتٰٮهُمَا ۚ فَتَعٰلَى اللّٰهُ عَمَّا يُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(190)\n\nBut when He giveth them a good child they ascribe unto Him partners in what He hath given them; but most exalted is God above what they associate (with Him).\nاَيُشْرِكُوْنَ مَا لَا يَخْلُقُ شَيْئًا وَّهُمْ يُخْلَقُوْنَ ۖ ‏(191)\n\nWhat! Do they associate (with Him) that which createth not anything, and while they are themselves the created (ones)?\nوَلَا يَسْتَطِيْعُوْنَ لَهُمْ نَصْرًا وَّلَاۤ اَنْفُسَهُمْ يَنْصُرُوْنَ‏(192)\n\nAnd they cannot help them, nor themselves can they help.\nوَاِنْ تَدْعُوْهُمْ اِلَى الْهُدٰى لَا يَتَّبِعُوْكُمْ ؕ سَوَآءٌ عَلَيْكُمْ اَدَعَوْتُمُوْهُمْ اَمْ اَنْتُمْ صٰمِتُوْنَ‏(193)\n\nIf ye invite them unto guidance they will not follow you; it is the same to you if ye invite them or ye be quiet.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ تَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ عِبَادٌ اَمْثَالُكُمْ فَادْعُوْهُمْ فَلْيَسْتَجِيْبُوْا لَكُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(194)\n\nVerily, those whom ye call upon other than God are subservient (to God) like unto your own selves, so call ye on them, then let them answer if ye be truthful.\nاَلَهُمْ اَرْجُلٌ يَّمْشُوْنَ بِهَآ اَمْ لَهُمْ اَيْدٍ يَّبْطِشُوْنَ بِهَآ اَمْ لَهُمْ اَعْيُنٌ يُّبْصِرُوْنَ بِهَآ اَمْ لَهُمْ اٰذَانٌ يَّسْمَعُوْنَ بِهَا ؕ قُلِ ادْعُوْا شُرَكَآءَكُمْ ثُمَّ كِيْدُوْنِ فَلَا تُنْظِرُوْنِ‏(195)\n\nWhat! are there for them feet which they walk with, Or for them are hands which they hold with, Or for them are eyes which they see with, or for them are ears which they hear with? Say (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “Call ye all your associates and then scheme ye (your worst) against me and give me no respite.\nاِنَّ وَلىِّۦَ اللّٰهُ الَّذِىْ نَزَّلَ الْكِتٰبَ ۖ  وَهُوَ يَتَوَلَّى الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(196)\n\nVerily my Protector is God Who sent down the Book (Qur’an) and He guardeth the virtuous ones.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ تَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِهٖ لَا يَسْتَطِيْعُوْنَ نَصْرَكُمْ وَلَاۤ اَنْفُسَهُمْ يَنْصُرُوْنَ‏(197)\n\nAnd those whom ye call upon other than Him are not able to help you, nor can they help themselves.\nوَاِنْ تَدْعُوْهُمْ اِلَى الْهُدٰى لَا يَسْمَعُوْا ؕ وَتَرٰٮهُمْ يَنْظُرُوْنَ اِلَيْكَ وَهُمْ لَا يُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(198)\n\nAnd if ye invite them unto guidance, they hear not; and thou seest them looking towards thee, while they see not.\nخُذِ الْعَفْوَ وَاْمُرْ بِالْعُرْفِ وَاَعْرِضْ عَنِ الْجٰهِلِيْنَ‏(199)\n\nAdopt thou moderation, and enjoin virtue and turn thou away from the ignorant ones.\nوَاِمَّا يَنْزَغَنَّكَ مِنَ الشَّيْطٰنِ نَزْغٌ فَاسْتَعِذْ بِاللّٰهِؕ اِنَّهٗ سَمِيْعٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(200)\n\nAnd if an incitement from the Satan inciteth thee, then seek thou refuge in God; Verily He is All-Hearing, All-Knowing.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اتَّقَوْا اِذَا مَسَّهُمْ طٰۤئِفٌ مِّنَ الشَّيْطٰنِ تَذَكَّرُوْا فَاِذَا هُمْ مُّبْصِرُوْنَۚ‏(201)\n\nVerily those who guard (themselves against evil) when an evil thought from the Satan afflicteth them, they become mindful (of God and get awakened) then lo! they see (aright).\nوَاِخْوَانُهُمْ يَمُدُّوْنَهُمْ فِى الْغَىِّ ثُمَّ لَا يُقْصِرُوْنَ‏(202)\n\nAnd their brethren drag them deeper into the error, so they cease not their efforts.\nوَاِذَا لَمْ تَاْتِهِمْ بِاٰيَةٍ قَالُوْا لَوْلَا اجْتَبَيْتَهَا ؕ قُلْ اِنَّمَاۤ اَتَّبِعُ مَا يُوْحٰٓى اِلَىَّ مِنْ رَّبِّىْ ۚ هٰذَا بَصَآئِرُ مِنْ رَّبِّكُمْ وَهُدًى وَّ رَحْمَةٌ لِّقَوْمٍ يُّؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(203)\n\nAnd when thou bringest not unto them a sign say they: “Why not thou forge it?” Say: “Verily I only follow what is revealed unto me from my Lord; these are clear proofs from your Lord, and a guidance, and a mercy for a people who believe.\nوَاِذَا قُرِئَ الْقُرْاٰنُ فَاسْتَمِعُوْا لَهٗ وَاَنْصِتُوْا لَعَلَّكُمْ تُرْحَمُوْنَ‏(204)\n\nAnd when the Qur’an is recited; then ye listen to it and be attentive, that mercy be done unto you.\nوَاذْكُرْ رَّبَّكَ فِىْ نَفْسِكَ تَضَرُّعًا وَّخِيْفَةً وَّدُوْنَ الْجَهْرِ مِنَ الْقَوْلِ بِالْغُدُوِّ وَالْاٰصَالِ وَلَا تَكُنْ مِّنَ الْغٰفِلِيْنَ‏(205)\n\nAnd remember thy Lord within thy self in humility and awe, and not aloud a voice, in the morning and the evening; and be thou not of the negligent ones.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ عِنْدَ رَبِّكَ لَا يَسْتَكْبِرُوْنَ عَنْ عِبَادَتِهٖ وَيُسَبِّحُوْنَهٗ وَلَهٗ يَسْجُدُوْنَ۩‏(206)\n\nVerily those who are with thy Lord, pride not to worship Him; they glorify Him and (in worship) unto Him they prostrate.",
  "merits": "There are 206 verses in this ‘Makki’ Surah. It is reported from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.), that whoever recites this Surah once a month, he will have no worry or fear on the Day of Resurrection and if it is recited on a Friday, then the reciter will be from among those who will be exempted from the taking of accounts on the Day of Judgement.\nSurah al-Aa’raaf has the Aayaat al-Mohkamaat that will give witness on behalf of its reciter on the Day of Reckoning. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that there will be a veil between the reciter of this Surah and Iblees on Judgement day and the reciter will be in the company of Prophet Adam (a.s.)\nWriting this Surah with rose water and saffron and keeping the writing at all times ensures safety from enemies and wild animals."
